window.I2_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Species & Biodiversity 物種與生物多樣性","cards":[{"w":"species","p":"n.","d":"a group of animals or plants of the same kind","c":"物種","s":"Scientists discovered a new species of frog in the mountains of Taiwan, and they are now studying how it survives the cold winters.","t":"科學家在台灣山區發現了一種新的青蛙物種，他們現在正在研究牠如何度過寒冷的冬天。"},{"w":"endangered","p":"adj.","d":"in danger of disappearing forever","c":"瀕臨絕種的","s":"The Formosan clouded leopard was once an endangered animal in Taiwan, but sadly no one has seen one in the wild for many years.","t":"台灣雲豹曾經是台灣瀕臨絕種的動物，但遺憾的是，已經很多年沒有人在野外見過牠了。"},{"w":"extinct","p":"adj.","d":"no longer existing anywhere in the world","c":"絕種的","s":"Dinosaurs have been extinct for about 66 million years, so we can only learn about them from fossils and bones.","t":"恐龍已經絕種大約六千六百萬年了，所以我們只能從化石和骨頭來認識牠們。"},{"w":"extinction","p":"n.","d":"the situation when a species no longer exists","c":"滅絕","s":"Many frogs around the world face extinction because a deadly disease is spreading quickly, and scientists are racing to find a cure.","t":"世界各地許多青蛙正面臨滅絕，因為一種致命的疾病正在迅速擴散，而科學家們正爭分奪秒地尋找解藥。"},{"w":"biodiversity","p":"n.","d":"the variety of plants and animals in one place","c":"生物多樣性","s":"Coral reefs have amazing biodiversity because thousands of fish and sea creatures live there, so protecting them is very important.","t":"珊瑚礁擁有驚人的生物多樣性，因為有成千上萬種魚類和海洋生物住在那裡，所以保護它們非常重要。"},{"w":"mammal","p":"n.","d":"an animal that feeds its babies with milk","c":"哺乳動物","s":"A whale looks like a giant fish, but it is actually a mammal because it breathes air and feeds its babies with milk.","t":"鯨魚看起來像一條巨大的魚，但牠其實是一種哺乳動物，因為牠呼吸空氣並用乳汁餵養寶寶。"},{"w":"reptile","p":"n.","d":"a cold-blooded animal with dry skin, like a snake","c":"爬蟲類動物","s":"A turtle is a reptile that lays its eggs on the beach, and the baby turtles must run to the sea after they hatch.","t":"烏龜是一種會在海灘上產卵的爬蟲類動物，而小海龜孵化後必須奔向大海。"},{"w":"amphibian","p":"n.","d":"an animal that lives both in water and on land","c":"兩棲動物","s":"A frog is an amphibian because it begins life in the water as a tadpole, but later it can also live on land.","t":"青蛙是一種兩棲動物，因為牠一開始以蝌蚪的形態生活在水中，但之後也能在陸地上生活。"},{"w":"primate","p":"n.","d":"a group of animals that includes monkeys, apes and humans","c":"靈長類動物","s":"The Formosan rock macaque is the only wild primate in Taiwan, and you can often see groups of them at Shoushan in Kaohsiung.","t":"台灣獼猴是台灣唯一的野生靈長類動物，你常常可以在高雄的壽山看到成群的牠們。"},{"w":"rodent","p":"n.","d":"a small animal with sharp front teeth, like a mouse","c":"囓齒動物","s":"A squirrel is a rodent with strong front teeth, so it can easily break open hard nuts and seeds in the forest.","t":"松鼠是一種前齒很強壯的囓齒動物，所以牠能輕易地咬開森林裡堅硬的堅果和種子。"},{"w":"marsupial","p":"n.","d":"an animal that carries its baby in a pouch","c":"有袋動物","s":"The kangaroo is the most famous marsupial in Australia, and the mother carries her tiny baby in a pouch for several months.","t":"袋鼠是澳洲最有名的有袋動物，而母袋鼠會把小小的寶寶放在育兒袋裡好幾個月。"},{"w":"carnivore","p":"n.","d":"an animal that eats meat","c":"肉食性動物","s":"A lion is a carnivore that hunts zebras and other large animals, so it needs to eat a lot of meat to stay strong.","t":"獅子是一種會獵捕斑馬和其他大型動物的肉食性動物，所以牠需要吃大量的肉才能保持強壯。"},{"w":"herbivore","p":"n.","d":"an animal that eats only plants","c":"草食性動物","s":"The giant panda is mostly a herbivore because it eats bamboo almost all day, although it sometimes eats small animals too.","t":"大貓熊大多是草食性動物，因為牠幾乎整天都在吃竹子，雖然牠偶爾也會吃小動物。"},{"w":"omnivore","p":"n.","d":"an animal that eats both plants and meat","c":"雜食性動物","s":"A bear is an omnivore that eats fruit, insects and fish, so it can find food easily in different seasons.","t":"熊是一種會吃水果、昆蟲和魚的雜食性動物，所以牠在不同季節都能輕易找到食物。"},{"w":"predator","p":"n.","d":"an animal that hunts and kills other animals","c":"掠食者","s":"The eagle is a powerful predator in the sky, and small birds hide in the bushes whenever they see its shadow.","t":"老鷹是天空中強大的掠食者，每當小鳥看到牠的影子就會躲進灌木叢裡。"},{"w":"prey","p":"n.","d":"an animal that is hunted and eaten by another","c":"獵物","s":"Rabbits are common prey for foxes and owls, so they always stay alert and run quickly when they hear a strange noise.","t":"兔子是狐狸和貓頭鷹常見的獵物，所以牠們總是保持警覺，一聽到奇怪的聲音就會快速逃跑。"},{"w":"vertebrate","p":"n.","d":"an animal that has a backbone","c":"脊椎動物","s":"Fish, birds and humans are all vertebrate because they have a backbone, but worms and jellyfish do not have one.","t":"魚、鳥和人類都是脊椎動物，因為牠們有脊椎骨，但蟲和水母則沒有。"},{"w":"invertebrate","p":"n.","d":"an animal without a backbone","c":"無脊椎動物","s":"An octopus is a clever invertebrate that has no bones at all, so it can squeeze through very small holes.","t":"章魚是一種聰明的無脊椎動物，牠完全沒有骨頭，所以能擠過非常小的洞。"},{"w":"subspecies","p":"n.","d":"a smaller group within a species","c":"亞種","s":"The Formosan black bear is a subspecies of the Asian black bear, and it has a white V-shaped mark on its chest.","t":"台灣黑熊是亞洲黑熊的一個亞種，牠的胸前有一個白色的V字形斑紋。"},{"w":"wildlife","p":"n.","d":"animals and plants that live in nature","c":"野生動植物","s":"Kenting National Park is full of wildlife, so visitors often see colourful birds, butterflies and even wild deer during their trip.","t":"墾丁國家公園充滿了野生動植物，所以遊客在旅途中常常能看見色彩繽紛的鳥、蝴蝶，甚至野鹿。"},{"w":"fauna","p":"n.","d":"all the animals living in a particular area","c":"動物群；某地區的動物","s":"The fauna of Madagascar is very special because about ninety percent of its animals cannot be found anywhere else on Earth.","t":"馬達加斯加的動物群非常特別，因為那裡大約百分之九十的動物在地球上其他地方都找不到。"},{"w":"flora","p":"n.","d":"all the plants growing in a particular area","c":"植物群；某地區的植物","s":"The guide explained the local flora to us during the hike, and we learned that some flowers only bloom in high mountains.","t":"嚮導在健行途中向我們介紹當地的植物，我們得知有些花只在高山上開花。"},{"w":"organism","p":"n.","d":"a living thing, such as a plant or animal","c":"生物；有機體","s":"Even the smallest organism in a pond plays a role in nature, because bigger animals depend on it for food.","t":"即使是池塘中最小的生物在大自然中也扮演一個角色，因為較大的動物依賴牠作為食物。"},{"w":"specimen","p":"n.","d":"an example of an animal or plant kept for study","c":"標本；樣本","s":"The museum keeps a specimen of an extinct bird in a glass box, so students can see what it looked like long ago.","t":"博物館把一隻已滅絕鳥類的標本保存在玻璃盒裡，讓學生們能看到牠很久以前的模樣。"},{"w":"rare","p":"adj.","d":"not seen or found very often","c":"稀有的","s":"The Mikado pheasant is a rare bird that lives only in Taiwan's high mountains, so photographers wait for hours to take its picture.","t":"帝雉是一種只生活在台灣高山的稀有鳥類，所以攝影師們會等上好幾個小時只為了拍到牠。"},{"w":"endemic","p":"adj.","d":"found naturally in only one place","c":"特有的","s":"The Taiwan blue magpie is endemic to Taiwan, which means you cannot see this beautiful bird in the wild in any other country.","t":"台灣藍鵲是台灣特有的鳥類，這表示你在其他任何國家的野外都看不到這種美麗的鳥。"},{"w":"indigenous","p":"adj.","d":"belonging naturally to a place; original","c":"原生的；本土的","s":"Farmers planted indigenous trees along the river instead of foreign ones, because local birds and insects depend on them.","t":"農夫們沿著河岸種植原生樹木而不是外來樹種，因為當地的鳥類和昆蟲依賴它們生存。"},{"w":"nocturnal","p":"adj.","d":"active at night and sleeping during the day","c":"夜行性的","s":"Owls are nocturnal birds that hunt mice in the dark, so you rarely see them flying around during the day.","t":"貓頭鷹是在黑暗中獵捕老鼠的夜行性鳥類，所以你很少在白天看到牠們飛來飛去。"},{"w":"flightless","p":"adj.","d":"not able to fly","c":"不會飛的","s":"The kakapo is a flightless parrot from New Zealand, so it walks and climbs trees instead of flying away from danger.","t":"鴞鸚鵡是一種來自紐西蘭的不會飛的鸚鵡，所以牠遇到危險時是用走和爬樹的方式，而不是飛走。"},{"w":"pollinator","p":"n.","d":"an insect or animal that carries pollen between flowers","c":"授粉者","s":"The bee is an important pollinator for many fruit trees, so farmers worry when the number of bees goes down.","t":"蜜蜂是許多果樹重要的授粉者，所以當蜜蜂數量減少時，農夫們就會擔心。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Habitats & Ecosystems 棲地與生態系","cards":[{"w":"habitat","p":"n.","d":"the natural home of an animal or plant","c":"棲地；棲息地","s":"When a forest is cut down, many animals lose their habitat, and they have to search for a new place to live.","t":"當森林被砍伐時，許多動物就失去了牠們的棲息地，而且必須尋找新的地方居住。"},{"w":"ecosystem","p":"n.","d":"all the living things in an area and how they connect","c":"生態系統","s":"If one animal disappears from an ecosystem, other animals and plants may also be affected because they all depend on each other.","t":"如果一種動物從一個生態系統中消失，其他動植物也可能受到影響，因為牠們都互相依賴。"},{"w":"ecology","p":"n.","d":"the study of how living things relate to their environment","c":"生態學","s":"My sister studies ecology at university, and she often goes to the wetlands to count birds and test the water.","t":"我姊姊在大學念生態學，她常常去濕地數鳥並檢測水質。"},{"w":"ecological","p":"adj.","d":"related to plants, animals and their environment","c":"生態的","s":"Building a new road through the forest could cause serious ecological damage, so many local people are against the plan.","t":"在森林中蓋一條新道路可能造成嚴重的生態破壞，所以許多當地居民反對這項計畫。"},{"w":"rainforest","p":"n.","d":"a thick tropical forest with heavy rain all year","c":"雨林","s":"The Amazon rainforest is home to millions of insects and animals, but large areas of it are cut down every year.","t":"亞馬遜雨林是數百萬種昆蟲和動物的家園，但每年都有大片面積遭到砍伐。"},{"w":"wetland","p":"n.","d":"land that is wet, such as a marsh or swamp","c":"濕地","s":"The black-faced spoonbills spend the winter in the wetland of Tainan, so many birdwatchers visit the area every year.","t":"黑面琵鷺在台南的濕地過冬，所以每年都有許多賞鳥人士造訪那個地區。"},{"w":"grassland","p":"n.","d":"a large area of land covered with grass","c":"草原","s":"Zebras and antelopes live on the African grassland, and they travel long distances every year to find fresh grass and water.","t":"斑馬和羚羊生活在非洲的草原上，牠們每年都要長途跋涉尋找新鮮的草和水。"},{"w":"savannah","p":"n.","d":"a flat grassy plain in a hot country with few trees","c":"熱帶大草原","s":"Lions rest under the trees of the savannah during the hot afternoon, and they usually hunt when the sun goes down.","t":"獅子在炎熱的午後於熱帶大草原的樹下休息，而牠們通常在太陽下山後才狩獵。"},{"w":"tundra","p":"n.","d":"a cold, flat area with no trees near the Arctic","c":"凍原；苔原","s":"The Arctic tundra is frozen for most of the year, but in summer it becomes green and many birds fly there to lay eggs.","t":"北極凍原一年中大部分時間都是冰凍的，但到了夏天就會變綠，許多鳥會飛到那裡產卵。"},{"w":"coral","p":"n.","d":"a hard sea substance made by tiny sea animals","c":"珊瑚","s":"When the sea becomes too warm, coral turns white and may die, so divers are worried about the future of the reefs.","t":"當海水變得太暖時，珊瑚會變白甚至死亡，所以潛水員們很擔心珊瑚礁的未來。"},{"w":"reef","p":"n.","d":"a line of rock or coral near the surface of the sea","c":"礁；暗礁","s":"We went snorkelling near a reef in Green Island, and we saw colourful fish swimming between the rocks.","t":"我們在綠島的一處珊瑚礁附近浮潛，看到了色彩繽紛的魚在岩石之間游來游去。"},{"w":"mangrove","p":"n.","d":"a tree that grows in salty water along coasts","c":"紅樹林","s":"The mangrove along the coast protect the land from strong waves, and they also give young fish a safe place to grow.","t":"海岸邊的紅樹林保護陸地免受大浪侵襲，同時也提供小魚一個安全成長的地方。"},{"w":"estuary","p":"n.","d":"the wide part of a river where it meets the sea","c":"河口","s":"The Danshui River estuary is full of crabs and birds, because fresh water and sea water mix there and bring plenty of food.","t":"淡水河河口充滿了螃蟹和鳥類，因為淡水和海水在那裡交會，帶來了豐富的食物。"},{"w":"canopy","p":"n.","d":"the top layer of branches and leaves in a forest","c":"樹冠層","s":"Many monkeys spend their whole lives in the forest canopy, so they rarely come down to the ground.","t":"許多猴子一生都待在森林的樹冠層，所以牠們很少下到地面上。"},{"w":"undergrowth","p":"n.","d":"bushes and small plants growing under big trees","c":"矮樹叢；下層灌木","s":"The small deer hid in the thick undergrowth when it heard our footsteps, so we could not take a photo of it.","t":"小鹿聽到我們的腳步聲就躲進了茂密的矮樹叢裡，所以我們沒辦法拍到牠的照片。"},{"w":"burrow","p":"n.","d":"a hole in the ground that an animal digs to live in","c":"地洞；洞穴","s":"The pangolin digs a deep burrow under the ground, and it sleeps there during the day to stay cool and safe.","t":"穿山甲在地底下挖了一個很深的洞穴，白天牠就在那裡睡覺，以保持涼爽和安全。"},{"w":"nest","p":"n.","d":"a home that birds build for their eggs","c":"巢；鳥巢","s":"A pair of swallows built a nest under our balcony, and we watched the parents feed their babies every morning.","t":"一對燕子在我們的陽台下築了一個巢，我們每天早上都看著燕子爸媽餵食牠們的寶寶。"},{"w":"den","p":"n.","d":"the hidden home of a wild animal such as a bear","c":"獸穴；巢穴","s":"The mother bear stays in her den all winter, and her cubs are born there while the snow covers the forest.","t":"熊媽媽整個冬天都待在她的巢穴裡，而當白雪覆蓋森林時，她的小熊就在那裡出生。"},{"w":"territory","p":"n.","d":"an area that an animal treats as its own","c":"領域；地盤","s":"A male tiger marks its territory with its smell, and it will fight any other tiger that tries to enter.","t":"公老虎會用氣味標示牠的地盤，而且會和任何試圖闖入的其他老虎打鬥。"},{"w":"niche","p":"n.","d":"the special role of a species in its environment","c":"生態棲位","s":"Each bird on the island has its own niche, because some eat seeds while others catch insects, so they do not compete for food.","t":"島上每種鳥都有自己的生態棲位，因為有些吃種子，有些捕捉昆蟲，所以牠們不會爭奪食物。"},{"w":"migration","p":"n.","d":"the seasonal movement of animals to another place","c":"遷徙","s":"The migration of the purple crow butterflies in Taiwan is famous, so the government closes some highway lanes to protect them every spring.","t":"台灣紫斑蝶的遷徙非常有名，所以政府每年春天都會封閉部分高速公路車道來保護牠們。"},{"w":"migrate","p":"v.","d":"to travel to another place when the season changes","c":"遷徙；遷移","s":"Gray-faced buzzards migrate through Kenting every autumn, and thousands of birdwatchers gather there to watch them fly across the sky.","t":"每年秋天灰面鵟鷹會遷徙經過墾丁，成千上萬的賞鳥人士聚集在那裡觀看牠們飛越天空。"},{"w":"hibernate","p":"v.","d":"to sleep through the whole winter","c":"冬眠","s":"Some bears hibernate during the cold months because food is hard to find, and they live on the fat stored in their bodies.","t":"有些熊會在寒冷的月份冬眠，因為食物很難找到，牠們靠著儲存在體內的脂肪維生。"},{"w":"hibernation","p":"n.","d":"a long sleep that some animals have in winter","c":"冬眠","s":"After a long hibernation, the hedgehog woke up very hungry, so it searched the garden for insects and worms.","t":"經過漫長的冬眠後，刺蝟醒來時非常飢餓，所以牠在花園裡四處尋找昆蟲和蟲子。"},{"w":"ecologist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies living things and their environment","c":"生態學家","s":"The ecologist spent three months in the mountains, and she recorded every type of bird she saw in her notebook.","t":"那位生態學家在山上待了三個月，她把看到的每一種鳥都記錄在筆記本上。"},{"w":"terrain","p":"n.","d":"an area of land and its physical features","c":"地形；地勢","s":"The rangers use horses instead of cars because the terrain is rocky and steep, and there are no proper roads.","t":"巡山員們騎馬而不是開車，因為那裡的地形多岩石又陡峭，而且沒有像樣的道路。"},{"w":"vegetation","p":"n.","d":"plants in general, especially in one area","c":"植被；植物","s":"After the heavy rain, the vegetation on the hills grew quickly, so the deer had plenty of fresh leaves to eat.","t":"大雨過後，山坡上的植被迅速生長，所以鹿有大量新鮮的葉子可以吃。"},{"w":"waterhole","p":"n.","d":"a pool of water where wild animals go to drink","c":"水坑；飲水處","s":"During the dry season, elephants walk for hours to reach a waterhole, but lions often wait there to catch other animals.","t":"在乾季時，大象要走好幾個小時才能到達水坑，但獅子常常在那裡等著捕捉其他動物。"},{"w":"marine","p":"adj.","d":"related to the sea and the animals in it","c":"海洋的","s":"Plastic bags are a serious danger to marine animals, because turtles often think the bags are jellyfish and eat them.","t":"塑膠袋對海洋動物是嚴重的危害，因為海龜常常把塑膠袋誤認為水母而吃下去。"},{"w":"scavenger","p":"n.","d":"an animal that eats dead animals it did not kill","c":"食腐動物","s":"The vulture is a scavenger that eats dead animals, so it helps to keep the savannah clean and stops diseases from spreading.","t":"禿鷹是一種吃動物屍體的食腐動物，所以牠幫助維持草原的乾淨，並防止疾病擴散。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Threats to Wildlife 野生動物面臨的威脅","cards":[{"w":"threat","p":"n.","d":"something that may cause harm or danger","c":"威脅","s":"Stray dogs are a serious threat to wild birds in the park, because they often chase and attack birds that nest on the ground.","t":"流浪狗對公園裡的野鳥是嚴重的威脅，因為牠們常常追逐並攻擊在地面築巢的鳥。"},{"w":"threaten","p":"v.","d":"to put something in danger","c":"威脅；危及","s":"Rising sea levels threaten the nesting beaches of sea turtles, and some beaches may disappear completely in the future.","t":"海平面上升威脅到海龜的築巢海灘，而有些海灘未來可能會完全消失。"},{"w":"deforestation","p":"n.","d":"the cutting down of forests on a large scale","c":"森林砍伐","s":"deforestation in Southeast Asia has destroyed the homes of orangutans, so their numbers have fallen sharply in the past thirty years.","t":"東南亞的森林砍伐摧毀了紅毛猩猩的家園，所以牠們的數量在過去三十年間急遽下降。"},{"w":"logging","p":"n.","d":"the business of cutting down trees for wood","c":"伐木","s":"Illegal logging continues in some national parks, because the wood is valuable and the forests are too large to guard.","t":"非法伐木在一些國家公園仍持續發生，因為木材很值錢，而森林又大到難以看守。"},{"w":"destruction","p":"n.","d":"the act of damaging something so badly it cannot be used","c":"破壞；毀滅","s":"The destruction of wetlands for new factories has left many birds with nowhere to rest during their long journey.","t":"為了蓋新工廠而破壞濕地，讓許多鳥類在漫長的旅程中無處歇息。"},{"w":"destroy","p":"v.","d":"to damage something so badly that it cannot be used","c":"摧毀；破壞","s":"The forest fire destroy thousands of trees last summer, and many koalas lost their homes and food.","t":"去年夏天的森林大火摧毀了數千棵樹，許多無尾熊因此失去了家園和食物。"},{"w":"fragmentation","p":"n.","d":"the breaking of a large area into small separate parts","c":"破碎化；分割","s":"Habitat fragmentation is a big problem for leopards, because new roads divide the forest into small pieces and the cats cannot meet each other.","t":"棲地破碎化對豹來說是個大問題，因為新道路把森林分割成小塊，使這些貓科動物無法彼此相遇。"},{"w":"encroach","p":"v.","d":"to slowly take over land that belongs to others","c":"侵占；侵入","s":"As cities grow, houses encroach on the forest, so monkeys sometimes come into people's kitchens to look for food.","t":"隨著城市擴張，房屋侵占了森林，所以猴子有時候會跑進人們的廚房找食物。"},{"w":"urbanisation","p":"n.","d":"the growth of towns and cities","c":"都市化","s":"Rapid urbanisation has replaced many rice fields with tall buildings, so frogs and egrets have fewer places to live.","t":"快速的都市化使許多稻田被高樓取代，所以青蛙和白鷺鷥能居住的地方變少了。"},{"w":"pesticide","p":"n.","d":"a chemical used to kill insects that harm crops","c":"殺蟲劑；農藥","s":"Farmers used too much pesticide on their vegetables, and as a result many bees and birds near the farm died.","t":"農夫們在蔬菜上使用了太多農藥，結果農場附近許多蜜蜂和鳥都死了。"},{"w":"poison","p":"v.","d":"to harm or kill with a dangerous substance","c":"毒害；下毒","s":"Some farmers poison rats in their fields, but owls and eagles then eat the dead rats and become sick.","t":"有些農夫在田裡毒殺老鼠，但貓頭鷹和老鷹接著吃了死老鼠就會生病。"},{"w":"contamination","p":"n.","d":"the process of making something dirty or harmful","c":"汙染","s":"Water contamination from a nearby factory killed hundreds of fish in the river, so the villagers asked the government to take action.","t":"附近工廠造成的水質汙染害死了河裡數百條魚，所以村民們要求政府採取行動。"},{"w":"contaminate","p":"v.","d":"to make something dirty or poisonous","c":"汙染","s":"Oil from the broken ship began to contaminate the beach, and volunteers rushed to clean the feathers of the seabirds.","t":"破損船隻漏出的油開始汙染海灘，志工們趕緊去清洗海鳥的羽毛。"},{"w":"plastic","p":"n.","d":"a light material made from chemicals, used for bags and bottles","c":"塑膠","s":"Scientists found pieces of plastic inside the stomach of a dead whale, so they asked people to stop using so many straws and bags.","t":"科學家在一隻死去的鯨魚胃裡發現了塑膠碎片，所以他們呼籲大家不要再使用那麼多吸管和塑膠袋。"},{"w":"debris","p":"n.","d":"broken pieces of rubbish that are left behind","c":"碎片；殘骸；垃圾","s":"After the typhoon, the beach was covered with debris, and a young turtle was found trapped in an old fishing net.","t":"颱風過後，海灘上布滿了垃圾碎片，還發現一隻小海龜被困在舊漁網裡。"},{"w":"invasive","p":"adj.","d":"spreading quickly and harming the local plants or animals","c":"入侵的；外來入侵的","s":"The green iguana is an invasive species in southern Taiwan, because it eats farmers' crops and has no natural enemies here.","t":"綠鬣蜥在台灣南部是一種外來入侵物種，因為牠會吃農作物，而且在這裡沒有天敵。"},{"w":"outbreak","p":"n.","d":"the sudden start of a disease","c":"爆發","s":"An outbreak of bird flu forced the zoo to close for two weeks, while the vets tested all the birds.","t":"禽流感的爆發迫使動物園關閉兩週，同時獸醫們為所有鳥類進行檢測。"},{"w":"starvation","p":"n.","d":"suffering or death caused by having no food","c":"飢餓；餓死","s":"Many polar bears face starvation because the sea ice melts earlier each year, so they cannot hunt seals for long enough.","t":"許多北極熊面臨餓死的危機，因為海冰每年都更早融化，所以牠們無法有足夠長的時間獵捕海豹。"},{"w":"starve","p":"v.","d":"to suffer or die because there is no food","c":"挨餓；餓死","s":"If the bamboo forests keep disappearing, the pandas will starve, because bamboo makes up almost all of their food.","t":"如果竹林持續消失，貓熊就會餓死，因為竹子幾乎是牠們全部的食物。"},{"w":"drought","p":"n.","d":"a long period with little or no rain","c":"乾旱","s":"The long drought dried up the rivers in Kenya, and hundreds of elephants died because they could not find water.","t":"漫長的乾旱使肯亞的河流乾涸，數百頭大象因為找不到水而死亡。"},{"w":"wildfire","p":"n.","d":"a large fire that spreads quickly in forests","c":"野火；森林大火","s":"The wildfire in Australia spread very fast because of the strong wind, and millions of animals could not escape in time.","t":"澳洲的野火因為強風而蔓延得非常快，數百萬隻動物來不及逃生。"},{"w":"overfishing","p":"n.","d":"catching too many fish so their number falls","c":"過度捕撈","s":"overfishing has made sharks much harder to find, because boats catch them faster than they can produce babies.","t":"過度捕撈讓鯊魚越來越難找到，因為漁船捕捉牠們的速度比牠們繁殖的速度還快。"},{"w":"bycatch","p":"n.","d":"sea animals caught by accident while fishing","c":"混獲；意外捕獲的漁獲","s":"Dolphins often become bycatch in large fishing nets, so some fishermen now use special nets that let them escape.","t":"海豚常常在大型漁網中成為混獲，所以有些漁民現在使用能讓牠們逃脫的特殊漁網。"},{"w":"collision","p":"n.","d":"an accident when two things hit each other","c":"碰撞；相撞","s":"A collision with a fast boat badly hurt the manatee, so the rescue team took it to an animal hospital.","t":"與快艇的碰撞讓那隻海牛受了重傷，所以救援團隊把牠送到動物醫院。"},{"w":"roadkill","p":"n.","d":"animals killed by cars on roads","c":"路殺","s":"roadkill is a big problem for leopard cats in Miaoli, so the government put up warning signs along the mountain roads.","t":"路殺對苗栗的石虎是一大問題，所以政府在山區道路沿線設置了警告標誌。"},{"w":"erosion","p":"n.","d":"the slow wearing away of land by water or wind","c":"侵蝕","s":"Beach erosion is making the turtles' nesting areas smaller, and the eggs may be washed away by big waves.","t":"海灘侵蝕正使海龜的築巢區域變小，而且蛋可能會被大浪沖走。"},{"w":"dwindle","p":"v.","d":"to become gradually smaller in number","c":"逐漸減少","s":"The number of wild tigers has dwindle over the last century, but some countries are now working hard to protect them.","t":"野生老虎的數量在過去一個世紀逐漸減少，但有些國家現在正努力保護牠們。"},{"w":"drain","p":"v.","d":"to remove the water from an area","c":"排乾（水）","s":"The company wanted to drain the marsh to build a parking lot, but the birdwatchers protested because thousands of birds rest there.","t":"那家公司想排乾沼澤的水來蓋停車場，但賞鳥人士提出抗議，因為有成千上萬隻鳥在那裡休息。"},{"w":"pollutant","p":"n.","d":"a substance that makes air, water or land dirty","c":"汙染物","s":"The factory released a dangerous pollutant into the river, and soon the fish and frogs began to disappear.","t":"那家工廠把一種危險的汙染物排進河裡，不久之後魚和青蛙就開始消失了。"},{"w":"vanish","p":"v.","d":"to disappear suddenly or completely","c":"消失","s":"Many small birds have vanish from the island since rats arrived on ships, because the rats eat their eggs.","t":"自從老鼠搭船來到島上後，許多小鳥就從島上消失了，因為老鼠會吃牠們的蛋。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Poaching & Illegal Wildlife Trade 盜獵與非法野生動物交易","cards":[{"w":"poach","p":"v.","d":"to hunt or catch animals illegally","c":"盜獵","s":"Criminals poach elephants for their tusks, and they sell the ivory for a lot of money in other countries.","t":"犯罪分子為了象牙盜獵大象，並將象牙在其他國家以高價賣出。"},{"w":"poacher","p":"n.","d":"a person who hunts animals illegally","c":"盜獵者","s":"The rangers caught a poacher in the national park last night, and they found three dead birds in his bag.","t":"巡山員昨晚在國家公園裡抓到一名盜獵者，並在他的袋子裡發現了三隻死鳥。"},{"w":"poaching","p":"n.","d":"the illegal hunting of animals","c":"盜獵（行為）","s":"poaching is the main reason why rhinos are in danger, because some people still believe their horns can cure illness.","t":"盜獵是犀牛陷入危險的主要原因，因為有些人仍然相信犀牛角能治病。"},{"w":"ivory","p":"n.","d":"the hard white material from elephant tusks","c":"象牙","s":"Many countries have stopped the sale of ivory, but some people still buy it secretly as jewellery or art.","t":"許多國家已經禁止販售象牙，但仍有一些人偷偷購買它作為珠寶或藝術品。"},{"w":"tusk","p":"n.","d":"a very long pointed tooth of an elephant","c":"（象等的）長牙","s":"An elephant uses its tusk to dig for water and remove tree bark, so losing them makes its life much harder.","t":"大象用牠的長牙挖水和剝樹皮，所以失去長牙會讓牠的生活困難許多。"},{"w":"horn","p":"n.","d":"a hard pointed part growing on an animal's head","c":"角","s":"A rhino's horn is made of the same material as our fingernails, but criminals still sell it at a very high price.","t":"犀牛的角是由和我們指甲一樣的物質組成，但犯罪分子仍以極高的價格販售它。"},{"w":"rhino","p":"n.","d":"a large heavy animal with one or two horns on its nose","c":"犀牛","s":"Only a few northern white rhino are left in the world, so scientists are trying to save them with new technology.","t":"全世界只剩下幾頭北方白犀牛，所以科學家們正嘗試用新科技拯救牠們。"},{"w":"pangolin","p":"n.","d":"a small animal covered in hard scales that eats ants","c":"穿山甲","s":"The pangolin rolls into a ball when it is scared, but this does not protect it from poachers who simply pick it up.","t":"穿山甲受到驚嚇時會捲成一顆球，但這無法保護牠免於盜獵者，因為他們直接就能把牠撿起來。"},{"w":"smuggle","p":"v.","d":"to take things secretly and illegally into a country","c":"走私","s":"The man tried to smuggle rare turtles through the airport in his suitcase, but the security officers found them on the X-ray screen.","t":"那名男子試圖把稀有的烏龜藏在行李箱裡走私通過機場，但安檢人員在X光螢幕上發現了牠們。"},{"w":"smuggler","p":"n.","d":"a person who smuggles goods illegally","c":"走私者","s":"The police arrested a smuggler at the harbour, because he was hiding hundreds of parrots in small plastic tubes.","t":"警方在港口逮捕了一名走私者，因為他把數百隻鸚鵡藏在小塑膠管裡。"},{"w":"trafficking","p":"n.","d":"the illegal buying and selling of goods or animals","c":"非法交易；販運","s":"Wildlife trafficking is a huge business around the world, so governments must work together to stop it.","t":"野生動物非法交易是全球性的大生意，所以各國政府必須合作阻止它。"},{"w":"trafficker","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys and sells illegal goods","c":"非法販運者","s":"The trafficker sold baby monkeys online as pets, but the police tracked him down after a buyer reported the website.","t":"那名非法販運者在網路上把小猴子當寵物販售，但在一位買家檢舉該網站後，警方追查到了他。"},{"w":"illegal","p":"adj.","d":"not allowed by law","c":"非法的；違法的","s":"It is illegal to keep a Formosan black bear as a pet in Taiwan, and anyone who does so may face a heavy fine.","t":"在台灣把台灣黑熊當寵物飼養是違法的，任何這麼做的人都可能面臨重罰。"},{"w":"confiscate","p":"v.","d":"to officially take something away from someone","c":"沒收","s":"Customs officers confiscate two hundred kilograms of shark fins, and they plan to destroy them in public next month.","t":"海關人員沒收了兩百公斤的魚翅，並計畫下個月公開銷毀。"},{"w":"seizure","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking illegal goods by force or law","c":"查獲；扣押","s":"The seizure of ten tonnes of pangolin scales was the largest ever in the country, and it shocked many animal lovers.","t":"查獲十公噸穿山甲鱗片是該國有史以來最大規模的查獲，讓許多愛護動物的人士大為震驚。"},{"w":"customs","p":"n.","d":"the place at a border where officers check goods","c":"海關","s":"The traveller was stopped at customs because his bag smelled strange, and the officers found live lizards inside.","t":"那名旅客在海關被攔下，因為他的包包有股奇怪的味道，而官員在裡面發現了活的蜥蜴。"},{"w":"ranger","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to protect a park or forest","c":"巡山員；保育巡查員","s":"The ranger walks through the forest every day to check the camera traps, and he also looks for signs of poachers.","t":"那位巡山員每天走過森林檢查自動相機，同時也尋找盜獵者的蹤跡。"},{"w":"patrol","p":"v.","d":"to walk or drive around an area to protect it","c":"巡邏","s":"Soldiers and rangers patrol the park at night, because most poachers come in the dark when they think no one is watching.","t":"士兵和巡山員晚上會在公園裡巡邏，因為大多數盜獵者會在他們以為沒人注意的夜裡前來。"},{"w":"trophy","p":"n.","d":"part of a dead animal kept to show hunting success","c":"（狩獵）戰利品","s":"Some rich tourists pay to shoot lions and take their heads home as a trophy, but many people think this is cruel.","t":"有些有錢的觀光客付錢射殺獅子，並把獅子頭帶回家當作戰利品，但許多人認為這很殘忍。"},{"w":"fur","p":"n.","d":"the thick soft hair of an animal","c":"毛皮","s":"Many fashion brands no longer use real fur in their coats, because customers do not want animals to suffer for clothes.","t":"許多時尚品牌不再在大衣中使用真的毛皮，因為顧客不希望動物為了衣服而受苦。"},{"w":"souvenir","p":"n.","d":"something you buy to remember a trip","c":"紀念品","s":"Never buy a souvenir made from coral or turtle shell on holiday, because it may be illegal and it harms sea life.","t":"度假時千萬不要購買用珊瑚或龜殼做的紀念品，因為那可能是違法的，而且會傷害海洋生物。"},{"w":"exotic","p":"adj.","d":"from a faraway country; unusual and interesting","c":"外來的；奇特的","s":"Some people keep exotic pets like snakes and parrots, but many of these animals were caught illegally in the wild.","t":"有些人飼養蛇和鸚鵡等奇特的寵物，但這些動物中有許多是從野外非法捕捉來的。"},{"w":"crackdown","p":"n.","d":"strong official action to stop illegal activity","c":"嚴厲打擊；取締","s":"The government started a crackdown on illegal pet shops, and dozens of rare birds were rescued in just one week.","t":"政府展開了對非法寵物店的嚴厲取締，短短一週內就救出了數十隻稀有鳥類。"},{"w":"penalty","p":"n.","d":"a punishment for breaking a law","c":"處罰；刑罰","s":"The penalty for killing a protected animal in Taiwan is very serious, and the criminal may even go to prison.","t":"在台灣殺害保育類動物的刑罰非常重，犯人甚至可能入獄。"},{"w":"snare","p":"n.","d":"a trap made of wire for catching animals","c":"（捕獸的）套索；陷阱","s":"A young bear lost part of its paw in a snare, so the vet had to perform an operation to save its life.","t":"一隻小熊的腳掌因捕獸套索失去了一部分，所以獸醫必須動手術救牠一命。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Conservation Action & Protected Areas 保育行動與保護區","cards":[{"w":"conserve","p":"v.","d":"to protect something from being damaged or lost","c":"保護；保存","s":"Local villagers work with scientists to conserve the forest, because it gives them clean water as well as a home for animals.","t":"當地村民和科學家合作保護森林，因為森林不僅為動物提供家園，也為他們提供乾淨的水。"},{"w":"conservationist","p":"n.","d":"a person who works to protect nature","c":"保育人士","s":"The conservationist has spent twenty years saving sea turtles, and she teaches children how to keep the beaches clean.","t":"那位保育人士花了二十年拯救海龜，她也教孩子們如何保持海灘乾淨。"},{"w":"preservation","p":"n.","d":"the act of keeping something safe from harm","c":"保存；保護","s":"The preservation of old forests is important, because many animals cannot survive in young forests that have just been planted.","t":"老森林的保護很重要，因為許多動物無法在剛種植的年輕森林中生存。"},{"w":"protection","p":"n.","d":"the act of keeping someone or something safe","c":"保護","s":"The black-faced spoonbill is under legal protection in Taiwan, so no one is allowed to hunt or disturb it.","t":"黑面琵鷺在台灣受到法律保護，所以任何人都不得獵捕或干擾牠。"},{"w":"sanctuary","p":"n.","d":"a safe place where animals are protected","c":"保護區；庇護所","s":"The elephants at the sanctuary were rescued from circuses, and now they can walk freely and swim in the river.","t":"庇護所裡的大象是從馬戲團被救出來的，現在牠們可以自由行走並在河裡游泳。"},{"w":"wilderness","p":"n.","d":"a wild natural area where no people live","c":"荒野","s":"Alaska still has huge areas of wilderness, so bears and wolves can live there without being disturbed by people.","t":"阿拉斯加仍有大片的荒野，所以熊和狼可以生活在那裡而不受人類干擾。"},{"w":"reintroduce","p":"v.","d":"to bring an animal back to an area where it once lived","c":"重新引入；野放回原棲地","s":"Scientists plan to reintroduce beavers to the river, because they believe the animals can help create new wetlands.","t":"科學家計畫把河狸重新引入那條河，因為他們相信這些動物能幫助創造新的濕地。"},{"w":"reintroduction","p":"n.","d":"the act of bringing a species back to its old habitat","c":"重新引入","s":"The reintroduction of wolves to Yellowstone was a great success, and the whole ecosystem became healthier afterwards.","t":"狼群重新引入黃石公園非常成功，之後整個生態系統都變得更健康了。"},{"w":"restoration","p":"n.","d":"the act of returning something to its earlier good condition","c":"復育；修復","s":"The restoration of the old rice fields brought back many frogs and fireflies, so families now visit the area at night.","t":"舊稻田的復育讓許多青蛙和螢火蟲回來了，所以現在家庭們都會在晚上造訪那個地區。"},{"w":"rewilding","p":"n.","d":"returning land to its natural wild state","c":"野化；再野化","s":"rewilding projects in Europe allow farmland to turn back into forest, and wild animals like bison have started to return.","t":"歐洲的再野化計畫讓農地恢復成森林，而像野牛這樣的野生動物已經開始回來了。"},{"w":"corridor","p":"n.","d":"a strip of land that connects two habitats","c":"（生態）廊道","s":"The government built a wildlife corridor under the highway, so leopard cats can cross safely from one forest to another.","t":"政府在高速公路下方建造了一條野生動物廊道，讓石虎能安全地從一片森林穿越到另一片森林。"},{"w":"quota","p":"n.","d":"a fixed limit on the number of something allowed","c":"配額；限額","s":"Each fishing boat has a quota for tuna, so it must stop fishing when it reaches that number.","t":"每艘漁船都有鮪魚的捕撈配額，所以達到該數量時就必須停止捕撈。"},{"w":"census","p":"n.","d":"an official count of a population","c":"普查；數量調查","s":"Volunteers joined the annual bird census last weekend, and they counted more spoonbills than ever before.","t":"志工們上週末參加了年度鳥類普查，他們數到的黑面琵鷺比以往任何時候都多。"},{"w":"tag","p":"v.","d":"to put a small label or device on an animal","c":"為……加上標籤","s":"Researchers tag young sharks with small electronic devices, so they can follow where the sharks swim around the world.","t":"研究人員為幼鯊加上小型電子標籤，這樣他們就能追蹤鯊魚在世界各地游到哪裡。"},{"w":"collar","p":"n.","d":"a band put around an animal's neck","c":"項圈","s":"The bear wears a GPS collar around its neck, and the scientists can see its location on their computer every hour.","t":"那隻熊的脖子上戴著一個GPS項圈，科學家每小時都能在電腦上看到牠的位置。"},{"w":"volunteer","p":"n.","d":"a person who works without being paid","c":"志工；義工","s":"As a volunteer at the animal rescue centre, I clean the cages every Saturday, and I also help feed the injured birds.","t":"身為動物救援中心的志工，我每個星期六都會清洗籠子，也會幫忙餵食受傷的鳥。"},{"w":"donation","p":"n.","d":"money or goods given to help a group","c":"捐款；捐贈","s":"Thanks to a large donation from a local company, the zoo was able to build a bigger home for its tigers.","t":"多虧一家本地公司的大筆捐款，動物園得以為老虎建造一個更大的家。"},{"w":"charity","p":"n.","d":"an organisation that helps people or animals in need","c":"慈善機構","s":"My class raised money for a wildlife charity, and the charity used it to buy medicine for injured turtles.","t":"我們班為一家野生動物慈善機構募款，而該機構用這筆錢購買受傷海龜的藥品。"},{"w":"campaign","p":"n.","d":"a planned series of actions to achieve a goal","c":"運動；宣傳活動","s":"The students started a campaign to stop people from feeding wild monkeys, because human food makes the monkeys sick and aggressive.","t":"學生們發起了一項宣傳活動，勸阻人們餵食野生猴子，因為人類的食物會讓猴子生病並變得具攻擊性。"},{"w":"petition","p":"n.","d":"a written request signed by many people","c":"請願書；連署","s":"More than fifty thousand people signed a petition to save the wetland, so the city council finally cancelled the building plan.","t":"超過五萬人簽署了拯救濕地的連署，所以市議會最終取消了建設計畫。"},{"w":"ecotourism","p":"n.","d":"travel to natural areas that helps protect them","c":"生態旅遊","s":"ecotourism brings money to local villages, so people there now see living whales as more valuable than dead ones.","t":"生態旅遊為當地村莊帶來收入，所以那裡的人們現在認為活的鯨魚比死的更有價值。"},{"w":"eco-friendly","p":"adj.","d":"not harmful to the environment","c":"環保的；對環境友善的","s":"Our hotel uses eco-friendly soap and shampoo, because the water from the rooms flows into a river full of fish.","t":"我們的飯店使用環保香皂和洗髮精，因為房間的排水會流入一條充滿魚的河流。"},{"w":"recovery","p":"n.","d":"the process of returning to a healthy state","c":"恢復；復原","s":"The humpback whale has made a strong recovery since hunting was stopped, and now tourists can see them near Taiwan again.","t":"自從捕鯨被禁止後，大翅鯨的數量已大幅恢復，現在遊客又能在台灣附近看到牠們了。"},{"w":"rebound","p":"v.","d":"to increase again after falling","c":"回升；反彈","s":"The number of sea otters began to rebound after hunting was banned, and today hundreds swim along the Californian coast.","t":"禁止獵捕後海獺的數量開始回升，如今已有數百隻在加州海岸游泳。"},{"w":"thrive","p":"v.","d":"to grow strongly and successfully","c":"茁壯成長；興盛","s":"Fireflies thrive in clean, dark places, so they disappear quickly when bright lights and dirty water arrive.","t":"螢火蟲在乾淨又黑暗的地方茁壯繁衍，所以當明亮的燈光和髒水出現時，牠們很快就會消失。"},{"w":"flourish","p":"v.","d":"to grow well and be healthy","c":"繁盛；蓬勃發展","s":"After the factory closed, the river became clean again, and fish and water birds began to flourish there.","t":"工廠關閉後，河水又變乾淨了，魚和水鳥開始在那裡繁盛起來。"},{"w":"treaty","p":"n.","d":"a formal written agreement between countries","c":"條約","s":"More than 180 countries have signed a treaty that controls the trade in wild animals, but some still fail to follow it.","t":"超過一百八十個國家簽署了一項管制野生動物貿易的條約，但有些國家仍未遵守。"},{"w":"cull","p":"v.","d":"to kill some animals to reduce their number","c":"撲殺；選擇性宰殺","s":"The island decided to cull the wild goats, because they were eating all the plants that rare birds needed.","t":"那座島決定撲殺野山羊，因為牠們把稀有鳥類需要的植物都吃光了。"},{"w":"relocate","p":"v.","d":"to move animals to a new place","c":"遷移；移置","s":"The team had to relocate the turtle eggs to a safer beach, because the old beach was going to flood during the typhoon.","t":"團隊必須把海龜蛋移置到較安全的海灘，因為原本的海灘在颱風期間將會淹水。"},{"w":"buffer","p":"n.","d":"an area that protects something from harm","c":"緩衝區","s":"Farmers left a buffer of trees between their fields and the river, and it stops chemicals from flowing into the water.","t":"農夫們在農田和河流之間留下一片樹木作為緩衝區，它能阻止化學物質流入水中。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Animal Behaviour, Breeding & Rescue 動物行為、繁殖與救援","cards":[{"w":"breed","p":"v.","d":"to keep animals so that they produce babies","c":"繁殖；培育","s":"The zoo has bred several baby pandas over the years, and some of them were later sent back to China.","t":"動物園多年來已經繁殖了好幾隻貓熊寶寶，其中有些後來被送回中國。"},{"w":"breeding","p":"n.","d":"the process of animals producing young","c":"繁殖；育種","s":"The breeding season for sea turtles starts in May, so the beaches are closed to visitors at night.","t":"海龜的繁殖季從五月開始，所以海灘晚上不開放遊客進入。"},{"w":"captive","p":"adj.","d":"kept in a cage or enclosed area; not free","c":"圈養的；被捕獲的","s":"The captive kakapos are watched closely by scientists, and each egg is carefully protected until it hatches.","t":"圈養的鴞鸚鵡受到科學家密切觀察，每一顆蛋都受到細心保護直到孵化。"},{"w":"captivity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being kept in a cage or zoo","c":"圈養；囚禁","s":"Dolphins in captivity often show signs of boredom, because a small pool is very different from the open ocean.","t":"圈養中的海豚常常出現無聊的跡象，因為小水池和廣闊的海洋非常不同。"},{"w":"offspring","p":"n.","d":"the baby or babies of an animal","c":"後代；幼崽","s":"An elephant usually has only one offspring every four or five years, so it takes a long time for their numbers to grow.","t":"大象通常每四到五年才生一隻後代，所以牠們的數量需要很長時間才能增加。"},{"w":"mate","p":"v.","d":"to come together to produce babies","c":"交配","s":"Male peacocks show their beautiful tails to attract females, and the females choose the best male to mate with.","t":"雄孔雀展示牠們美麗的尾羽來吸引雌孔雀，而雌孔雀會選擇最好的雄孔雀來交配。"},{"w":"hatch","p":"v.","d":"to break out of an egg","c":"孵化","s":"The baby turtles hatch at night when the sand is cool, and then they follow the moonlight to the sea.","t":"小海龜在沙子涼爽的夜晚孵化，然後牠們跟著月光爬向大海。"},{"w":"hatchling","p":"n.","d":"a baby animal that has just come out of its egg","c":"剛孵化的幼體","s":"Only one hatchling out of a thousand turtles grows into an adult, because birds and fish eat most of them.","t":"一千隻剛孵化的小海龜中只有一隻能長大為成龜，因為大部分都被鳥和魚吃掉了。"},{"w":"cub","p":"n.","d":"a young bear, lion, tiger or fox","c":"幼獸（熊、獅、虎等）","s":"The bear cub stays with its mother for about two years, and it learns how to find food and climb trees.","t":"小熊會和媽媽待在一起大約兩年，學習如何找食物和爬樹。"},{"w":"calf","p":"n.","d":"a young cow, elephant or whale","c":"幼崽（牛、象、鯨等）","s":"The baby elephant is called a calf, and the whole herd protects it when lions come close.","t":"小象被稱為幼象，當獅子靠近時，整個象群都會保護牠。"},{"w":"litter","p":"n.","d":"a group of baby animals born at the same time","c":"一窩（幼崽）","s":"Our neighbour's cat gave birth to a litter of five kittens, so she is looking for kind families to adopt them.","t":"鄰居的貓生了一窩五隻小貓，所以她正在尋找有愛心的家庭來領養牠們。"},{"w":"lay","p":"v.","d":"to produce an egg from the body","c":"產（卵）；下（蛋）","s":"The mother turtle laid about one hundred eggs in the sand, and then she slowly crawled back to the sea.","t":"海龜媽媽在沙裡產下大約一百顆蛋，然後慢慢地爬回大海。"},{"w":"incubate","p":"v.","d":"to keep eggs warm until they hatch","c":"孵（蛋）","s":"Because the parents had left the nest, the rescue centre had to incubate the eggs in a warm machine.","t":"因為鳥爸媽離開了鳥巢，救援中心只好用保溫機器來孵這些蛋。"},{"w":"forage","p":"v.","d":"to search for food","c":"覓食","s":"Wild boars forage in the forest at night, but sometimes they come into villages and dig up farmers' sweet potatoes.","t":"山豬在夜晚於森林中覓食，但有時牠們會跑進村莊挖農夫的地瓜。"},{"w":"graze","p":"v.","d":"to eat grass in a field","c":"吃草；放牧","s":"The deer graze quietly in the field every evening, but they run away as soon as they smell a human.","t":"鹿每天傍晚都在田野裡安靜地吃草，但一聞到人類的氣味就會立刻逃跑。"},{"w":"camouflage","p":"n.","d":"colours or patterns that help an animal hide","c":"偽裝；保護色","s":"The leaf insect has perfect camouflage, so birds fly right past it without noticing it on the branch.","t":"葉䗛有完美的偽裝，所以鳥從牠旁邊飛過也不會注意到樹枝上的牠。"},{"w":"instinct","p":"n.","d":"a natural behaviour an animal does without learning","c":"本能","s":"Baby turtles move towards the sea by instinct, even though no one has ever shown them the way.","t":"小海龜靠著本能朝大海前進，即使從來沒有人教過牠們怎麼走。"},{"w":"flock","p":"n.","d":"a group of birds or sheep","c":"（鳥或羊的）群","s":"A flock of spoonbills landed in the wetland at sunset, and the birdwatchers quickly lifted their cameras.","t":"一群黑面琵鷺在日落時降落在濕地上，賞鳥人士迅速舉起了相機。"},{"w":"herd","p":"n.","d":"a large group of animals such as cows or elephants","c":"（動物的）群","s":"A herd of buffalo crossed the road slowly, so all the cars had to stop and wait for several minutes.","t":"一群水牛緩緩地穿越馬路，所以所有車輛都必須停下來等好幾分鐘。"},{"w":"solitary","p":"adj.","d":"living or spending time alone","c":"獨居的","s":"Leopards are solitary animals that hunt alone, while lions live and hunt together in big family groups.","t":"豹是單獨狩獵的獨居動物，而獅子則以大家庭群體一起生活和狩獵。"},{"w":"rescue","p":"v.","d":"to save someone or something from danger","c":"救援；拯救","s":"Fishermen rescue a baby dolphin that was trapped in a net, and they carefully returned it to the sea.","t":"漁民們救出了一隻被困在網中的小海豚，並小心地把牠送回海裡。"},{"w":"rehabilitate","p":"v.","d":"to help an injured animal become healthy again","c":"使康復；使復原","s":"The centre rehabilitate injured eagles for several months, and then it releases them back into the mountains.","t":"中心會花好幾個月幫助受傷的老鷹康復，然後把牠們野放回山林。"},{"w":"rehabilitation","p":"n.","d":"the process of helping an animal recover","c":"復健；康復治療","s":"After three months of rehabilitation, the sea turtle could swim well again, so the vets returned it to the ocean.","t":"經過三個月的復健，那隻海龜又能好好游泳了，所以獸醫們把牠放回海洋。"},{"w":"veterinarian","p":"n.","d":"an animal doctor","c":"獸醫","s":"The veterinarian removed a fishing hook from the bird's throat, and the bird was able to eat again the next day.","t":"獸醫從那隻鳥的喉嚨裡取出了一個魚鉤，隔天那隻鳥就能再次進食了。"},{"w":"orphaned","p":"adj.","d":"having lost its parents","c":"失去父母的；成為孤兒的","s":"The orphaned baby monkey was found alone by the road, so volunteers fed it milk every three hours.","t":"那隻失去父母的小猴子被發現獨自待在路邊，所以志工們每三個小時就餵牠喝一次奶。"},{"w":"injured","p":"adj.","d":"hurt or harmed","c":"受傷的","s":"We found an injured owl in the school garden, and we called the animal rescue centre right away.","t":"我們在學校的花園裡發現了一隻受傷的貓頭鷹，於是馬上打電話給動物救援中心。"},{"w":"zookeeper","p":"n.","d":"a person who looks after animals in a zoo","c":"動物園管理員；保育員","s":"The zookeeper prepares fresh bamboo for the pandas every morning, and she also checks whether they are healthy.","t":"那位保育員每天早上都為貓熊準備新鮮的竹子，也會檢查牠們是否健康。"},{"w":"enclosure","p":"n.","d":"an area with a fence or wall where animals are kept","c":"圍欄；圈養區","s":"The new enclosure for the tigers has trees, rocks and a pool, so the animals can behave more naturally.","t":"老虎的新圈養區有樹木、岩石和水池，所以動物們能表現得更自然。"},{"w":"aquarium","p":"n.","d":"a building where people can see fish and sea animals","c":"水族館","s":"We visited the aquarium in Pingtung last summer, and the children loved watching the penguins and sharks.","t":"我們去年夏天參觀了屏東的水族館，孩子們很喜歡看企鵝和鯊魚。"},{"w":"zoo","p":"n.","d":"a place where wild animals are kept for people to see","c":"動物園","s":"The Taipei zoo is very popular with families, and it also runs programmes to protect the Formosan pangolin.","t":"台北市立動物園很受家庭歡迎，而且它也推行保護台灣穿山甲的計畫。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"People, Farming & Wildlife Conflict 人類、畜牧與野生動物衝突","cards":[{"w":"livestock","p":"n.","d":"farm animals such as cows, sheep and goats","c":"家畜；牲畜","s":"Wolves sometimes attack farmers' livestock at night, so many farmers now use guard dogs to protect their sheep.","t":"狼有時會在夜裡攻擊農夫的家畜，所以許多農夫現在用護衛犬來保護他們的羊。"},{"w":"cattle","p":"n.","d":"cows and bulls kept on a farm","c":"牛（總稱）","s":"The farmer lost three cattle to a lion last month, so he is now building a stronger fence around his farm.","t":"那位農夫上個月有三頭牛被獅子咬死，所以他現在正在農場周圍建造更堅固的圍籬。"},{"w":"herder","p":"n.","d":"a person who looks after a group of animals","c":"牧民；牧人","s":"The herder walks with his goats through the mountains every day, and he carries a whistle to scare away wild animals.","t":"那位牧民每天帶著他的山羊走過山區，並帶著一個哨子來嚇跑野生動物。"},{"w":"rancher","p":"n.","d":"a person who owns or runs a large cattle farm","c":"牧場主人","s":"The rancher was angry when wolves returned to the area, but later he learned to protect his cows without killing them.","t":"當狼回到這個地區時，那位牧場主人很生氣，但後來他學會了在不殺狼的情況下保護他的牛。"},{"w":"farmland","p":"n.","d":"land used for growing crops or keeping animals","c":"農地；農田","s":"Much of the forest was turned into farmland fifty years ago, so the leopard cats now live close to people.","t":"五十年前大部分的森林被改成了農地，所以石虎現在住得離人很近。"},{"w":"crop","p":"n.","d":"a plant grown on a farm for food","c":"農作物","s":"Elephants sometimes eat a whole field of crop in one night, so the farmers lose all the food they planned to sell.","t":"大象有時一個晚上就吃掉整片田的農作物，讓農夫們失去所有打算拿去賣的作物。"},{"w":"fence","p":"n.","d":"a wall made of wood or wire around a field","c":"圍籬；柵欄","s":"The villagers built an electric fence around their fields, but the clever elephants learned to push trees onto it.","t":"村民們在田地周圍建造了電圍籬，但聰明的大象學會了把樹推倒在上面。"},{"w":"shepherd","p":"n.","d":"a person who looks after sheep","c":"牧羊人","s":"The shepherd keeps his sheep inside a strong pen at night, because snow leopards often hunt in the area.","t":"那位牧羊人晚上把羊關在堅固的羊圈裡，因為雪豹常在那一帶獵食。"},{"w":"raid","p":"v.","d":"to attack a place suddenly to take things","c":"襲擊；搶奪","s":"Monkeys often raid the fruit farms in the mountains, and they can eat hundreds of bananas in a single afternoon.","t":"猴子常常襲擊山上的果園，牠們一個下午就能吃掉數百根香蕉。"},{"w":"retaliate","p":"v.","d":"to hurt someone because they hurt you","c":"報復","s":"When a tiger killed their cows, some villagers wanted to retaliate, but the rangers convinced them to wait for help.","t":"當老虎咬死他們的牛時，有些村民想要報復，但巡山員說服他們等待協助。"},{"w":"retaliation","p":"n.","d":"action taken to hurt someone who hurt you","c":"報復（行為）","s":"Many lions are killed in retaliation for attacks on cattle, so conservation groups pay farmers when they lose animals.","t":"許多獅子因為攻擊牛隻而遭到報復殺害，所以保育團體會在農民損失牲畜時給予賠償。"},{"w":"compensation","p":"n.","d":"money paid to someone for a loss","c":"補償；賠償金","s":"The government gives compensation to farmers whose chickens are killed by leopard cats, so the farmers are less likely to hurt them.","t":"政府會給雞隻被石虎咬死的農民賠償金，所以農民比較不會傷害石虎。"},{"w":"coexist","p":"v.","d":"to live together peacefully in the same place","c":"共存","s":"People and bears can coexist in the same mountains, but campers must keep their food in locked boxes.","t":"人類和熊可以在同一片山林中共存，但露營者必須把食物放在上鎖的箱子裡。"},{"w":"coexistence","p":"n.","d":"the state of living together peacefully","c":"共存","s":"Peaceful coexistence between farmers and elephants is possible, but it needs good planning and support from the government.","t":"農民與大象之間的和平共存是可能的，但這需要良好的規劃和政府的支持。"},{"w":"deter","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from happening by making it difficult","c":"嚇阻；阻止","s":"Farmers hang bright lights around their farms to deter lions at night, and the number of attacks has dropped a lot.","t":"農民在農場周圍掛上明亮的燈來在夜間嚇阻獅子，攻擊事件的數量因此大幅減少。"},{"w":"deterrent","p":"n.","d":"something that makes people or animals not want to do something","c":"嚇阻物；威懾","s":"Beehives along the fence are a good deterrent against elephants, because the large animals are afraid of bee stings.","t":"沿著圍籬設置的蜂箱是防範大象的好嚇阻物，因為這些大型動物害怕被蜜蜂叮咬。"},{"w":"trap","p":"n.","d":"a device for catching animals","c":"陷阱；捕獸器","s":"The researchers used a safe trap to catch the leopard cat, and they released it after putting on a GPS collar.","t":"研究人員用安全的捕獸器捕捉石虎，並在為牠戴上GPS項圈後將牠野放。"},{"w":"pest","p":"n.","d":"an insect or animal that damages crops or food","c":"害蟲；有害動物","s":"Some farmers see wild boars as a pest, because the boars destroy their vegetable gardens almost every night.","t":"有些農民把山豬視為有害動物，因為山豬幾乎每晚都破壞他們的菜園。"},{"w":"landowner","p":"n.","d":"a person who owns land","c":"地主","s":"The landowner agreed to keep part of his forest untouched, so the rare birds living there would not lose their home.","t":"那位地主同意保留他一部分的森林不被開發，讓住在那裡的稀有鳥類不會失去家園。"},{"w":"villager","p":"n.","d":"a person who lives in a village","c":"村民","s":"Every villager was invited to the meeting about the new nature park, because the plan would change their daily lives.","t":"每一位村民都受邀參加有關新自然公園的會議，因為這項計畫將會改變他們的日常生活。"},{"w":"harvest","p":"n.","d":"the time when crops are collected","c":"收成；收穫","s":"Just before the harvest, a group of monkeys came down from the mountain and ate most of the farmer's peaches.","t":"就在收成前，一群猴子從山上下來，吃掉了農夫大部分的桃子。"},{"w":"livelihood","p":"n.","d":"the way someone earns money to live","c":"生計","s":"Fishing is the main livelihood of the islanders, so they need to protect the sea if they want to keep their jobs.","t":"捕魚是島民主要的生計，所以如果他們想保住工作，就必須保護海洋。"},{"w":"poultry","p":"n.","d":"chickens, ducks and other farm birds","c":"家禽","s":"Leopard cats sometimes steal poultry from farms, but some farmers now use stronger cages to keep their chickens safe.","t":"石虎有時會偷農場的家禽，但有些農民現在用更堅固的籠子來保護他們的雞。"},{"w":"hostile","p":"adj.","d":"unfriendly and ready to fight","c":"敵對的；不友善的","s":"Local people used to be hostile towards the wolves, but their attitude changed when wolf tourism brought money to the town.","t":"當地人過去對狼抱持敵對的態度，但當賞狼旅遊為小鎮帶來收入後，他們的態度就改變了。"},{"w":"tolerate","p":"v.","d":"to accept something you do not like","c":"容忍；忍受","s":"Farmers are more willing to tolerate wild animals on their land when they receive help to protect their crops.","t":"當農民獲得保護農作物的協助時，他們更願意容忍野生動物出現在自己的土地上。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 1 (abandon – complement)","cards":[{"w":"abandon","p":"v.","d":"to leave something or someone and not come back","c":"拋棄；放棄","s":"Some owners abandon their pet turtles in city ponds when they get bored, but these turtles can harm the local wildlife.","t":"有些飼主玩膩了就把寵物烏龜棄養在城市池塘裡，但這些烏龜會危害當地的野生動物。"},{"w":"accompany","p":"v.","d":"to go somewhere with someone","c":"陪同；伴隨","s":"A trained guide will accompany every group into the forest, because visitors might get lost or disturb the nesting birds.","t":"每一團進入森林時都會有一位受過訓練的嚮導陪同，因為遊客可能會迷路或打擾築巢的鳥。"},{"w":"adjacent","p":"adj.","d":"next to or near something","c":"鄰近的；毗連的","s":"The new factory will be built on land adjacent to the wetland, so many birdwatchers are worried about noise and dirty water.","t":"新工廠將蓋在鄰近濕地的土地上，所以許多賞鳥人士擔心噪音和汙水的問題。"},{"w":"advocate","p":"v.","d":"to publicly support an idea or plan","c":"提倡；擁護","s":"Many scientists advocate stronger laws against the pet trade, because they have seen how many animals die during transport.","t":"許多科學家提倡更嚴格的法律來對抗寵物交易，因為他們親眼看到許多動物在運送途中死亡。"},{"w":"amend","p":"v.","d":"to make small changes to a law or document","c":"修訂；修正","s":"The government decided to amend the wildlife law last year, so the penalties for selling protected animals are now much heavier.","t":"政府去年決定修訂野生動物保育法，所以現在販售保育類動物的刑罰重了許多。"},{"w":"annual","p":"adj.","d":"happening once every year","c":"每年的；年度的","s":"The annual bird festival in Kenting attracts thousands of visitors, and local hotels are usually fully booked that week.","t":"墾丁一年一度的賞鳥節吸引了數千名遊客，當地的飯店那一週通常都會客滿。"},{"w":"arbitrary","p":"adj.","d":"chosen by chance, not based on reason","c":"任意的；武斷的","s":"The borders of the national park are not arbitrary, because scientists drew them after studying where the animals actually live.","t":"國家公園的邊界並不是任意劃定的，因為科學家們是在研究動物實際棲息的地點之後才畫出來的。"},{"w":"assemble","p":"v.","d":"to gather together in one place","c":"集合；聚集","s":"Thousands of crabs assemble on the beach every summer to release their eggs, and the road is closed so cars do not crush them.","t":"每年夏天成千上萬隻螃蟹會聚集在海灘上釋放卵，道路會因此封閉以免車子壓死牠們。"},{"w":"assess","p":"v.","d":"to judge how good, bad or serious something is","c":"評估","s":"Experts came to assess the damage after the oil spill, and they found that hundreds of seabirds had been affected.","t":"專家們在漏油事件後前來評估損害，他們發現有數百隻海鳥受到影響。"},{"w":"assign","p":"v.","d":"to give someone a job or task","c":"分配；指派","s":"The leader will assign each volunteer to a different beach, so the whole coastline can be checked for turtle nests.","t":"領隊會把每位志工分派到不同的海灘，這樣整條海岸線都能被檢查是否有海龜巢。"},{"w":"attain","p":"v.","d":"to reach a goal after a lot of effort","c":"達到；獲得","s":"The project hopes to attain its goal of five hundred kakapos by 2030, but it will need more money and more islands.","t":"該計畫希望在2030年前達到五百隻鴞鸚鵡的目標，但這需要更多資金和更多島嶼。"},{"w":"bulk","p":"n.","d":"the main or largest part of something","c":"大部分；主體","s":"The bulk of the money goes to paying rangers, because protecting the animals on the ground is the most important job.","t":"大部分的經費都用來支付巡山員的薪水，因為在第一線保護動物是最重要的工作。"},{"w":"capable","p":"adj.","d":"having the ability to do something","c":"有能力的；能夠的","s":"Crows are capable of using tools to find food, so scientists believe they are one of the smartest birds in the world.","t":"烏鴉能夠使用工具尋找食物，所以科學家們認為牠們是世界上最聰明的鳥類之一。"},{"w":"cease","p":"v.","d":"to stop doing something","c":"停止","s":"The factory was ordered to cease all work near the river, because its waste water was killing the fish.","t":"那家工廠被下令停止在河邊的所有作業，因為它的廢水正在殺死魚群。"},{"w":"cite","p":"v.","d":"to mention something as proof or an example","c":"引用；舉出","s":"In her report, the student cite a study about bees, and she used it to show why pesticides should be controlled.","t":"那位學生在報告中引用了一篇關於蜜蜂的研究，並用它來說明為何應該管制農藥。"},{"w":"coherent","p":"adj.","d":"clear, logical and easy to understand","c":"條理清晰的；連貫的","s":"The country needs a coherent plan to protect its forests, because different offices are currently making different rules.","t":"這個國家需要一套條理清楚的計畫來保護森林，因為目前不同單位制定了不同的規則。"},{"w":"coincide","p":"v.","d":"to happen at the same time as something else","c":"同時發生；巧合","s":"The rainy season coincide with the birth of many baby animals, so there is plenty of fresh food for the young ones.","t":"雨季和許多小動物出生的時間同時發生，所以幼小的動物有充足的新鮮食物。"},{"w":"collapse","p":"n.","d":"a sudden failure or fall","c":"崩潰；瓦解","s":"Scientists warned that the collapse of the fish population could happen quickly, so the fishing season was shortened.","t":"科學家警告魚群數量的崩潰可能來得很快，所以漁季被縮短了。"},{"w":"commence","p":"v.","d":"to begin","c":"開始","s":"The turtle-watching tours will commence in June, but visitors must book early because only twenty people can join each night.","t":"賞海龜行程將於六月開始，但遊客必須提早預約，因為每晚只能有二十人參加。"},{"w":"commission","p":"n.","d":"an official group given a special task","c":"委員會","s":"A special commission was set up to study the falling number of whales, and it will report its findings next year.","t":"一個特別委員會已經成立，專門研究鯨魚數量下降的問題，並將在明年公布調查結果。"},{"w":"commit","p":"v.","d":"to promise to give time or money to something","c":"承諾；投入","s":"The company has commit one million dollars to save the coral reefs, and its staff will also help clean the beaches.","t":"那家公司已承諾投入一百萬美元拯救珊瑚礁，員工們也會協助清理海灘。"},{"w":"commodity","p":"n.","d":"a product that can be bought and sold","c":"商品；貨物","s":"For some criminals, wild animals are just a commodity to sell, and they do not care if the animals suffer.","t":"對某些罪犯來說，野生動物只是可以販賣的商品，他們並不在乎動物是否受苦。"},{"w":"compatible","p":"adj.","d":"able to exist together without problems","c":"相容的；可共存的","s":"Tourism and wildlife protection can be compatible, but only if the number of visitors is carefully controlled.","t":"觀光和野生動物保護可以是相容的，但前提是遊客數量必須受到謹慎控管。"},{"w":"compile","p":"v.","d":"to collect information and put it together","c":"彙編；收集整理","s":"The volunteers compile a list of every bird they saw this year, and the list will help scientists study changes in the area.","t":"志工們彙整了今年看到的每一種鳥的清單，這份清單將幫助科學家研究這個地區的變化。"},{"w":"complement","p":"v.","d":"to add something that makes another thing better","c":"補充；與……相輔相成","s":"Online classes complement the field trips well, because students first learn the facts and then see the animals in real life.","t":"線上課程和戶外教學相輔相成，因為學生先學習知識，然後再親眼看到動物。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 2 (comprise – device)","cards":[{"w":"comprise","p":"v.","d":"to consist of or be made up of","c":"包含；由……組成","s":"The national park comprise forests, rivers and high mountains, so it is home to many different kinds of animals.","t":"這座國家公園包含森林、河流和高山，所以它是許多不同種類動物的家園。"},{"w":"conceive","p":"v.","d":"to think of a new idea or plan","c":"構想出；想出","s":"The idea of the wildlife bridge was conceive by a group of students, and the city later decided to build it.","t":"野生動物天橋的點子是由一群學生構想出來的，市政府後來決定建造它。"},{"w":"conduct","p":"v.","d":"to organise and carry out an activity","c":"進行；實施","s":"The university will conduct a study on the frogs in the area, because their numbers have fallen in recent years.","t":"大學將針對這個地區的青蛙進行一項研究，因為牠們的數量近年來下降了。"},{"w":"confine","p":"v.","d":"to keep someone or something within a small area","c":"限制；侷限","s":"The circus used to confine the tigers to small cages, but now the animals live in a large sanctuary.","t":"馬戲團過去把老虎關在小籠子裡，但現在這些動物住在一個大型庇護所中。"},{"w":"conform","p":"v.","d":"to follow rules or standards","c":"遵守；符合","s":"All new buildings near the coast must conform to the new rules, so they cannot use bright lights that confuse baby turtles.","t":"海岸附近所有的新建築都必須符合新規定，所以不能使用會讓小海龜迷失方向的強光。"},{"w":"constitute","p":"v.","d":"to form or make up something","c":"構成；組成","s":"Insects constitute more than half of all known animal species, but most people rarely think about protecting them.","t":"昆蟲構成了所有已知動物物種的一半以上，但大多數人很少想到要保護牠們。"},{"w":"construct","p":"v.","d":"to build something","c":"建造；建構","s":"Engineers construct a fish ladder beside the dam, so salmon can swim up the river to lay their eggs.","t":"工程師們在水壩旁建造了一座魚梯，讓鮭魚能逆流而上去產卵。"},{"w":"consult","p":"v.","d":"to ask an expert for advice or information","c":"諮詢；請教","s":"The city should consult wildlife experts before building the new road, because it will cross an important forest.","t":"市政府在建造新道路之前應該諮詢野生動物專家，因為這條路將穿越一片重要的森林。"},{"w":"contemporary","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to the present time; modern","c":"當代的；現代的","s":"contemporary zoos focus more on education and protection, while old zoos were mainly places for entertainment.","t":"當代的動物園更重視教育和保護，而舊式動物園主要是娛樂場所。"},{"w":"contrary","p":"adj.","d":"completely different or opposite","c":"相反的","s":"contrary to popular belief, sharks rarely attack humans, and many more sharks are killed by people every year.","t":"和一般人的看法相反，鯊魚很少攻擊人類，而每年被人類殺死的鯊魚卻多得多。"},{"w":"controversy","p":"n.","d":"a lot of public disagreement about something","c":"爭議","s":"The plan to kill wild cats on the island caused great controversy, because some people believed there were kinder solutions.","t":"撲殺島上野貓的計畫引起了極大的爭議，因為有些人認為還有更人道的解決方法。"},{"w":"convert","p":"v.","d":"to change something into a different form or use","c":"轉換；改變用途","s":"The town convert an old fish farm into a nature park, and now hundreds of birds stop there in winter.","t":"小鎮把一座舊養殖場改建成自然公園，現在每年冬天都有數百隻鳥在那裡停留。"},{"w":"convince","p":"v.","d":"to make someone believe or do something","c":"說服；使相信","s":"The documentary convince many viewers to stop eating shark fin soup, because it showed how cruel the fishing was.","t":"那部紀錄片說服了許多觀眾不再吃魚翅湯，因為它呈現了捕撈過程有多殘忍。"},{"w":"coordinate","p":"v.","d":"to organise people to work together well","c":"協調","s":"The centre coordinate the work of rangers, vets and volunteers, so every injured animal gets help as quickly as possible.","t":"中心負責協調巡山員、獸醫和志工的工作，讓每隻受傷的動物都能盡快獲得協助。"},{"w":"core","p":"n.","d":"the most central or important part","c":"核心；中心部分","s":"No visitors are allowed in the core of the reserve, because the rarest birds build their nests there.","t":"保護區的核心區域禁止遊客進入，因為最稀有的鳥類在那裡築巢。"},{"w":"corporate","p":"adj.","d":"related to large companies","c":"企業的；公司的","s":"More corporate sponsors are supporting wildlife projects, because customers prefer brands that care about nature.","t":"越來越多企業贊助商支持野生動物計畫，因為消費者偏好關心大自然的品牌。"},{"w":"correspond","p":"v.","d":"to match or be similar to something","c":"符合；相對應","s":"The drop in bird numbers correspond closely with the increase in pesticide use, so scientists believe the two are connected.","t":"鳥類數量的下降和農藥使用量的增加密切對應，所以科學家認為兩者有關聯。"},{"w":"criteria","p":"n.","d":"standards used to judge something","c":"標準；準則（複數）","s":"A species must meet certain criteria before it is called endangered, such as a fast drop in its population.","t":"一個物種必須符合某些標準才會被列為瀕危物種，例如族群數量快速下降。"},{"w":"cycle","p":"n.","d":"a series of events that happen again and again","c":"循環；週期","s":"The life cycle of a salmon is amazing, because it is born in a river, lives in the sea and returns to the same river.","t":"鮭魚的生命週期很驚人，因為牠在河中出生，在海裡生活，然後再回到同一條河。"},{"w":"deduce","p":"v.","d":"to reach a conclusion from the facts you have","c":"推斷；推論","s":"From the footprints in the mud, the ranger deduce that a mother bear and two cubs had passed by that morning.","t":"從泥巴上的腳印，巡山員推斷當天早上有一隻熊媽媽和兩隻小熊經過。"},{"w":"deny","p":"v.","d":"to say that something is not true","c":"否認","s":"The shop owner deny selling illegal birds, but the police found several rare parrots hidden in the back room.","t":"店主否認販售非法鳥類，但警方在後面的房間裡發現了好幾隻被藏起來的稀有鸚鵡。"},{"w":"deplete","p":"v.","d":"to use up or greatly reduce the amount of something","c":"耗盡；大量減少","s":"Overfishing has deplete the tuna in this part of the ocean, so the fishermen now have to sail much farther to catch anything.","t":"過度捕撈已經耗盡了這片海域的鮪魚，所以漁民現在必須航行得更遠才能捕到魚。"},{"w":"detect","p":"v.","d":"to notice or discover something","c":"偵測；察覺","s":"Hidden cameras can detect animals that move at night, so scientists can study shy creatures without disturbing them.","t":"隱藏式相機能偵測到夜間活動的動物，所以科學家可以在不打擾牠們的情況下研究害羞的生物。"},{"w":"deviate","p":"v.","d":"to move away from the usual way or plan","c":"偏離","s":"Visitors must not deviate from the marked path, because rare plants and small animals live on the forest floor.","t":"遊客不可以偏離標示的步道，因為稀有植物和小動物生活在森林地面上。"},{"w":"device","p":"n.","d":"a small machine or tool made for a purpose","c":"裝置；設備","s":"The scientists attached a tiny device to the turtle's shell, and it sends its location to a satellite every day.","t":"科學家在海龜的殼上裝了一個微小的裝置，它每天都會把位置傳送到衛星上。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 3 (devote – formula)","cards":[{"w":"devote","p":"v.","d":"to give your time or energy to something","c":"致力於；奉獻","s":"Jane Goodall devote her whole life to studying chimpanzees, and she taught the world how intelligent they are.","t":"珍古德把她的一生都奉獻給黑猩猩的研究，她讓全世界知道牠們有多聰明。"},{"w":"displace","p":"v.","d":"to force people or animals to leave their home","c":"迫使離開；取代","s":"The new dam displace hundreds of families and animals, because the water covered the whole valley.","t":"新水壩迫使數百個家庭和動物離開家園，因為水淹沒了整個山谷。"},{"w":"dispose","p":"v.","d":"to get rid of something","c":"處理；丟棄","s":"Campers must dispose of their rubbish properly, because bears and monkeys are attracted to the smell of food.","t":"露營者必須妥善處理垃圾，因為熊和猴子會被食物的氣味吸引。"},{"w":"distort","p":"v.","d":"to change facts so they are no longer true","c":"扭曲；曲解","s":"Some websites distort the facts about sharks to get more clicks, so many people are more afraid than they need to be.","t":"有些網站為了獲得更多點閱而扭曲關於鯊魚的事實，使許多人產生不必要的恐懼。"},{"w":"distribute","p":"v.","d":"to give things to many people","c":"分發；分配","s":"The volunteers distribute leaflets at the night market, and they explained why people should not buy wild animals.","t":"志工們在夜市發放傳單，並解釋為什麼人們不應該購買野生動物。"},{"w":"document","p":"v.","d":"to record information in writing or with photos","c":"記錄","s":"The photographer has document the life of a wild leopard family for five years, and his pictures are now in a book.","t":"那位攝影師已經記錄一個野生豹家庭的生活五年了，他的照片現在已出版成書。"},{"w":"domestic","p":"adj.","d":"kept by people at home or on a farm; tame","c":"家養的；馴化的","s":"domestic cats kill millions of wild birds every year, so experts suggest keeping pet cats indoors.","t":"家貓每年殺死數百萬隻野鳥，所以專家建議把寵物貓養在室內。"},{"w":"dominate","p":"v.","d":"to have the most power or importance","c":"支配；主宰","s":"In the forest, one strong male gorilla dominate the group, and the others follow him when he moves.","t":"在森林裡，一隻強壯的雄性大猩猩主宰整個群體，當牠移動時其他成員都會跟隨。"},{"w":"duration","p":"n.","d":"the length of time something lasts","c":"持續時間；期間","s":"For the duration of the nesting season, dogs are not allowed on the beach, because they may dig up the eggs.","t":"在築巢季的期間，狗不可以進入海灘，因為牠們可能會把蛋挖出來。"},{"w":"dynamic","p":"adj.","d":"always changing and full of energy","c":"動態的；充滿活力的","s":"A forest is a dynamic system that changes every season, so scientists must visit it many times a year.","t":"森林是一個每季都在改變的動態系統，所以科學家一年必須造訪許多次。"},{"w":"emphasis","p":"n.","d":"special importance given to something","c":"強調；重點","s":"The new programme puts great emphasis on education, because children who love nature will protect it when they grow up.","t":"新計畫非常重視教育，因為熱愛自然的孩子長大後會保護它。"},{"w":"encounter","p":"n.","d":"a meeting that is unexpected","c":"偶遇；邂逅","s":"My encounter with a wild bear on the mountain trail was frightening, but I stayed calm and slowly walked away.","t":"我在山路上和一隻野生熊的不期而遇很可怕，但我保持冷靜並慢慢地走開。"},{"w":"entity","p":"n.","d":"something that exists as a single unit","c":"實體；個體","s":"The river and the forest should be seen as one entity, because what happens to the water also affects the trees and animals.","t":"河流與森林應該被視為一個整體，因為水發生的事也會影響樹木和動物。"},{"w":"erode","p":"v.","d":"to slowly damage or wear away","c":"侵蝕；逐漸削弱","s":"Strong waves continue to erode the island's beaches, and soon there may be no sand left for turtles to nest in.","t":"強浪持續侵蝕島上的海灘，不久之後可能就沒有沙子讓海龜築巢了。"},{"w":"exceed","p":"v.","d":"to be more than a limit or amount","c":"超過；超出","s":"The number of tourists exceed the park's limit last weekend, so the rangers had to close the gate early.","t":"上週末遊客人數超過了公園的上限，所以巡山員不得不提早關閉大門。"},{"w":"exclude","p":"v.","d":"to keep out or not include","c":"排除；把……排除在外","s":"A special fence exclude foxes and cats from the area, so the small birds can raise their chicks safely.","t":"一道特殊的圍籬把狐狸和貓排除在這個區域之外，讓小鳥們能安全地養育雛鳥。"},{"w":"exhibit","p":"n.","d":"an object or display shown in a museum or zoo","c":"展覽品；展示","s":"The new exhibit at the museum shows the bones of a giant whale, and it also explains why whales need protection.","t":"博物館的新展覽展示了一頭巨鯨的骨骼，同時也說明了為什麼鯨魚需要保護。"},{"w":"expose","p":"v.","d":"to put someone or something in danger","c":"使暴露於；使接觸","s":"Cutting down the trees expose the soil to heavy rain, so the land quickly washes away into the river.","t":"砍伐樹木會使土壤暴露在大雨之下，所以土地很快就被沖進河裡。"},{"w":"external","p":"adj.","d":"coming from outside","c":"外部的","s":"external threats such as new roads and farms are pushing the animals into a smaller and smaller area.","t":"新道路和農場等外部威脅正把動物們逼進越來越小的區域。"},{"w":"extract","p":"v.","d":"to take something out, often with effort","c":"提取；開採","s":"Companies want to extract oil from under the Arctic ice, but scientists warn that a spill could kill many seals and whales.","t":"企業想從北極冰層下開採石油，但科學家警告漏油可能會害死許多海豹和鯨魚。"},{"w":"feature","p":"n.","d":"an important part or quality of something","c":"特色；特徵","s":"The long neck is the most famous feature of the giraffe, and it helps the animal eat leaves high up in the trees.","t":"長脖子是長頸鹿最有名的特徵，它幫助這種動物吃到樹上高處的葉子。"},{"w":"flexible","p":"adj.","d":"able to change easily","c":"有彈性的；靈活的","s":"Conservation plans must be flexible, because the weather and the animals' behaviour can change from year to year.","t":"保育計畫必須有彈性，因為天氣和動物的行為每年都可能改變。"},{"w":"fluctuate","p":"v.","d":"to go up and down often","c":"波動；起伏","s":"The number of butterflies fluctuate from year to year, so scientists need data from many years to see the real trend.","t":"蝴蝶的數量每年都會波動，所以科學家需要多年的資料才能看出真正的趨勢。"},{"w":"format","p":"n.","d":"the way something is arranged or presented","c":"格式；形式","s":"The wildlife report is available in a simple format for students, so even young readers can understand the main ideas.","t":"這份野生動物報告有提供給學生的簡易格式版本，所以即使是年紀小的讀者也能了解主要內容。"},{"w":"formula","p":"n.","d":"a special mix of ingredients","c":"配方","s":"The zoo developed a special milk formula for the baby pangolin, because its mother could not feed it.","t":"動物園為小穿山甲研發了一種特殊的奶粉配方，因為牠的媽媽無法餵養牠。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 4 (foundation – layer)","cards":[{"w":"foundation","p":"n.","d":"an organisation that gives money to good causes","c":"基金會","s":"The foundation gives money to schools that teach children about wildlife, and it also supports rangers in Africa.","t":"那個基金會捐款給教導孩子認識野生動物的學校，同時也支持非洲的巡山員。"},{"w":"generate","p":"v.","d":"to produce or create something","c":"產生；創造","s":"Whale watching generate a lot of income for the small fishing town, so the local people now protect the whales.","t":"賞鯨為這個小漁村創造了大量收入，所以當地人現在都保護鯨魚。"},{"w":"global","p":"adj.","d":"related to the whole world","c":"全球的","s":"The loss of bees is a global problem, so countries need to share their research and work together.","t":"蜜蜂消失是一個全球性的問題，所以各國需要分享研究並共同合作。"},{"w":"grant","p":"n.","d":"money given by a government or group for a purpose","c":"補助金；獎助金","s":"The team received a large grant from the government, so they can now buy cameras to study the leopard cats.","t":"團隊從政府獲得了一大筆補助金，所以他們現在能購買相機來研究石虎。"},{"w":"guarantee","p":"v.","d":"to promise that something will happen","c":"保證；確保","s":"No one can guarantee that the baby rhino will survive, but the vets are doing everything they can to help it.","t":"沒有人能保證那隻犀牛寶寶能活下來，但獸醫們正盡一切所能地幫助牠。"},{"w":"hierarchy","p":"n.","d":"a system where some members have more power than others","c":"階級；等級制度","s":"Wolves live in a clear hierarchy, and the strongest pair usually leads the pack and eats first.","t":"狼生活在明確的階級制度中，而最強壯的一對通常帶領狼群並最先進食。"},{"w":"ignorance","p":"n.","d":"lack of knowledge about something","c":"無知；不了解","s":"Many people harm wild animals out of ignorance rather than cruelty, so education is an important part of conservation.","t":"許多人傷害野生動物是出於無知而非殘忍，所以教育是保育中很重要的一環。"},{"w":"incentive","p":"n.","d":"something that encourages people to do something","c":"誘因；激勵","s":"The government offers farmers an incentive to plant trees on their land, so more birds have places to live.","t":"政府提供農民在自己的土地上種樹的誘因，讓更多鳥類有地方居住。"},{"w":"income","p":"n.","d":"money that someone earns","c":"收入","s":"Selling honey gives the villagers a steady income, so they no longer need to cut down the forest for money.","t":"販售蜂蜜為村民帶來穩定的收入，所以他們不再需要砍伐森林來賺錢。"},{"w":"individual","p":"n.","d":"a single person or animal","c":"個體；個人","s":"Scientists can recognise each individual whale by the shape of its tail, so they know which whales return every year.","t":"科學家能從尾巴的形狀辨認出每一隻鯨魚個體，所以他們知道哪些鯨魚每年都會回來。"},{"w":"inhibit","p":"v.","d":"to slow down or stop something","c":"抑制；阻礙","s":"Cold water can inhibit the growth of young fish, so the hatchery keeps the water at a warm temperature.","t":"冷水會抑制幼魚的成長，所以孵化場會把水溫維持在溫暖的溫度。"},{"w":"initiate","p":"v.","d":"to start something such as a plan","c":"發起；開始實施","s":"The school initiate a project to plant trees along the river, and every student planted one tree on Earth Day.","t":"學校發起了一項沿著河岸種樹的計畫，每位學生都在世界地球日種下一棵樹。"},{"w":"initiative","p":"n.","d":"a new plan to solve a problem","c":"倡議；新措施","s":"The city's new initiative turns off street lights near the beach at night, so baby turtles can find their way to the sea.","t":"市政府的新措施在夜間關閉海灘附近的路燈，讓小海龜能找到通往大海的路。"},{"w":"insight","p":"n.","d":"a deep and clear understanding of something","c":"洞察；深刻見解","s":"The study gave scientists new insight into how elephants talk to each other, because it recorded sounds too low for humans to hear.","t":"這項研究讓科學家對大象如何彼此溝通有了新的見解，因為它錄下了低到人類聽不見的聲音。"},{"w":"inspect","p":"v.","d":"to look at something carefully to check it","c":"檢查；視察","s":"Officers inspect every pet shop in the city twice a year, and they check whether any animals are illegal.","t":"官員每年兩次檢查市內的每家寵物店，確認是否有任何非法動物。"},{"w":"instance","p":"n.","d":"an example of something","c":"例子；實例","s":"In one instance, a dog found forty turtle nests in a single morning, so the team now trains more dogs for this job.","t":"在一個例子中，一隻狗在一個早上就找到了四十個海龜巢，所以團隊現在訓練更多的狗來做這項工作。"},{"w":"integral","p":"adj.","d":"necessary and important as part of a whole","c":"不可或缺的；構成整體所必需的","s":"Local people are an integral part of the project, because they know the forest better than anyone else.","t":"當地居民是這項計畫不可或缺的一部分，因為他們比任何人都更了解這片森林。"},{"w":"integrity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being whole and not damaged","c":"完整性","s":"The new highway would destroy the integrity of the forest, because it would cut the animals' home into two parts.","t":"新高速公路會破壞森林的完整性，因為它會把動物的家園切成兩半。"},{"w":"intense","p":"adj.","d":"very strong or extreme","c":"強烈的；劇烈的","s":"The intense heat this summer dried up many ponds, so the frogs had to find new places to lay their eggs.","t":"今年夏天強烈的高溫使許多池塘乾涸，所以青蛙們必須找新的地方產卵。"},{"w":"intensify","p":"v.","d":"to become stronger or more serious","c":"加強；加劇","s":"The police have intensify their checks at the airport, because more smugglers are trying to bring in rare reptiles.","t":"警方已加強機場的檢查，因為越來越多走私者試圖帶入稀有的爬蟲類。"},{"w":"internal","p":"adj.","d":"inside something such as a body or group","c":"內部的","s":"The vet used an X-ray to check for internal injuries, because the turtle had been hit by a boat but looked fine outside.","t":"獸醫用X光檢查是否有內部傷害，因為那隻海龜被船撞到了，但外表看起來沒事。"},{"w":"isolate","p":"v.","d":"to separate someone or something from others","c":"隔離；孤立","s":"The sick birds were isolate from the others in a separate room, so the disease would not spread through the whole zoo.","t":"生病的鳥被隔離在另一個房間，這樣疾病就不會傳遍整個動物園。"},{"w":"issue","p":"n.","d":"an important problem that people discuss","c":"議題；問題","s":"Plastic in the ocean has become a major issue in many countries, and some cities have stopped giving out free plastic bags.","t":"海洋中的塑膠已成為許多國家的重大議題，有些城市已經停止提供免費塑膠袋。"},{"w":"label","p":"v.","d":"to describe someone or something with a word","c":"把……稱為；貼上標籤","s":"People often label sharks as dangerous killers, but most sharks are shy and have never attacked a human.","t":"人們常常把鯊魚貼上危險殺手的標籤，但大多數鯊魚都很害羞，而且從未攻擊過人類。"},{"w":"layer","p":"n.","d":"a level of something that lies over or under another","c":"層","s":"Whales have a thick layer of fat under their skin, so they can stay warm even in very cold water.","t":"鯨魚的皮膚下有一層厚厚的脂肪，所以即使在非常冰冷的水中也能保暖。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 5 (link – phase)","cards":[{"w":"link","p":"n.","d":"a connection between two things","c":"關聯；連結","s":"Scientists found a clear link between warmer seas and the death of corals, so they are asking for faster action on climate.","t":"科學家發現海水變暖與珊瑚死亡之間有明顯的關聯，所以他們呼籲更快採取氣候行動。"},{"w":"locate","p":"v.","d":"to find the exact position of something","c":"找出……的位置","s":"The team used a drone to locate the missing bear, and they found it resting near a river two kilometres away.","t":"團隊用無人機找到了失蹤熊的位置，發現牠在兩公里外的河邊休息。"},{"w":"logic","p":"n.","d":"a sensible way of thinking","c":"邏輯；道理","s":"There is simple logic behind protecting bees, because without them, many of our fruits and vegetables would not grow.","t":"保護蜜蜂背後有個簡單的道理，因為沒有牠們，我們的許多水果和蔬菜就無法生長。"},{"w":"manual","p":"n.","d":"a book that tells you how to do something","c":"手冊；指南","s":"Every new volunteer receives a manual that explains how to handle injured birds, so they do not hurt the animals by mistake.","t":"每位新志工都會收到一本手冊，說明如何處理受傷的鳥，以免他們不小心傷害到動物。"},{"w":"margin","p":"n.","d":"the edge of an area","c":"邊緣","s":"Many birds nest along the margin of the lake, so boats are not allowed close to the shore in spring.","t":"許多鳥類沿著湖的邊緣築巢，所以春天時船隻不得靠近岸邊。"},{"w":"mental","p":"adj.","d":"related to the mind","c":"心理的；精神的","s":"Animals in small cages can suffer from mental problems, so good zoos give them toys and puzzles to keep them busy.","t":"關在小籠子裡的動物可能會出現心理問題，所以好的動物園會給牠們玩具和益智遊戲讓牠們保持忙碌。"},{"w":"minimal","p":"adj.","d":"very small in amount","c":"極少的；最小的","s":"The new tourist boats make minimal noise, so they do not frighten the dolphins swimming nearby.","t":"新型觀光船只發出極小的噪音，所以不會嚇到附近游泳的海豚。"},{"w":"motive","p":"n.","d":"the reason why someone does something","c":"動機","s":"Money is the main motive for most poachers, so helping villagers find other jobs can reduce hunting.","t":"金錢是大多數盜獵者的主要動機，所以幫助村民找到其他工作可以減少獵捕。"},{"w":"mutual","p":"adj.","d":"shared by two or more people or animals","c":"互相的；共同的","s":"The clownfish and the sea anemone have a mutual relationship, because each one helps the other to survive.","t":"小丑魚和海葵之間有一種互利的關係，因為彼此都幫助對方生存。"},{"w":"neutral","p":"adj.","d":"not supporting either side in a disagreement","c":"中立的","s":"The meeting was led by a neutral expert, so both the farmers and the conservation group felt their voices were heard.","t":"會議由一位中立的專家主持，所以農民和保育團體都覺得自己的聲音被聽見了。"},{"w":"nonetheless","p":"adv.","d":"however; even so","c":"儘管如此；然而","s":"The project faced many problems in its first year; nonetheless, the team managed to save twenty baby turtles.","t":"這項計畫在第一年遇到許多問題；儘管如此，團隊還是成功救了二十隻小海龜。"},{"w":"norm","p":"n.","d":"what is usual or expected","c":"常態；規範","s":"Using reusable bags has become the norm in many cities, and as a result less plastic ends up in the sea.","t":"使用環保袋在許多城市已成為常態，因此流入海洋的塑膠變少了。"},{"w":"notion","p":"n.","d":"an idea or belief","c":"觀念；概念","s":"The notion that zoos only exist for fun is out of date, because many zoos now help save endangered animals.","t":"動物園只是為了娛樂而存在的觀念已經過時了，因為現在許多動物園都在幫助拯救瀕危動物。"},{"w":"obtain","p":"v.","d":"to get something, often with effort","c":"取得；獲得","s":"Researchers must obtain a special permit before they enter the protected area, and they must follow strict rules inside.","t":"研究人員必須先取得特別許可才能進入保護區，而且在裡面必須遵守嚴格的規定。"},{"w":"obvious","p":"adj.","d":"easy to see or understand","c":"明顯的","s":"It was obvious that the bird was sick, because it could not stand up and its feathers were dirty.","t":"那隻鳥顯然生病了，因為牠無法站起來，羽毛也很髒。"},{"w":"occupy","p":"v.","d":"to live in or use a place","c":"占據；居住於","s":"The owls occupy an old building on the farm, and the farmer is happy because they catch the rats in his barn.","t":"貓頭鷹占據了農場上的一棟舊建築，農夫很高興，因為牠們會抓穀倉裡的老鼠。"},{"w":"occur","p":"v.","d":"to happen","c":"發生","s":"Most attacks on livestock occur at night, so farmers now bring their animals into safe pens before dark.","t":"大部分對家畜的攻擊都發生在夜晚，所以農民現在會在天黑前把動物趕進安全的圍欄。"},{"w":"offset","p":"v.","d":"to balance one thing with another","c":"抵銷；彌補","s":"The airline plants trees to offset the pollution from its flights, but some experts say this is not enough.","t":"那家航空公司種樹來抵銷航班造成的汙染，但有些專家說這樣還不夠。"},{"w":"ongoing","p":"adj.","d":"still happening; continuing","c":"進行中的；持續的","s":"The ongoing study of the bears has lasted ten years, and it has taught us a lot about their eating habits.","t":"對熊持續進行的研究已經持續了十年，它讓我們對牠們的飲食習慣了解很多。"},{"w":"option","p":"n.","d":"a choice you can make","c":"選擇；選項","s":"Moving the elephants to another park was the only option, because there was no longer enough food for them.","t":"把大象遷到另一座公園是唯一的選擇，因為那裡已經沒有足夠的食物給牠們了。"},{"w":"overall","p":"adj.","d":"including everything; general","c":"整體的；全面的","s":"The overall number of storks has increased this year, although some smaller groups are still in danger.","t":"今年鸛鳥的整體數量增加了，雖然有些較小的群體仍處於危險之中。"},{"w":"overseas","p":"adj.","d":"in or from another country across the sea","c":"海外的；國外的","s":"overseas visitors love Taiwan's mountain birds, so guided birdwatching tours have become a popular business.","t":"海外遊客很喜愛台灣的高山鳥類，所以導覽賞鳥行程已成為熱門的生意。"},{"w":"parallel","p":"adj.","d":"happening at the same time and similar","c":"平行的；同時進行的","s":"The two countries are running parallel programmes to protect the same turtles, because the turtles swim between both coasts.","t":"兩國正在進行平行的計畫來保護同一種海龜，因為這些海龜在兩國海岸之間游動。"},{"w":"persist","p":"v.","d":"to continue to exist for a long time","c":"持續存在","s":"Chemicals from old pesticides can persist in the soil for many years, so they still harm insects and birds today.","t":"舊農藥中的化學物質可以在土壤中持續存在很多年，所以至今仍會傷害昆蟲和鳥類。"},{"w":"phase","p":"n.","d":"a stage in a process","c":"階段","s":"In the first phase of the project, the team will count the animals, and in the second they will plant new trees.","t":"在計畫的第一階段，團隊將清點動物數量，第二階段則將種植新的樹木。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 6 (policy – reluctant)","cards":[{"w":"policy","p":"n.","d":"a plan of action agreed by a government or group","c":"政策","s":"The new policy bans single-use plastic in national parks, so visitors must bring their own bottles and bags.","t":"新政策禁止在國家公園使用一次性塑膠，所以遊客必須自備水瓶和袋子。"},{"w":"portion","p":"n.","d":"a part of something larger","c":"部分","s":"A large portion of the money from ticket sales is used to protect the forest, so visiting the park also helps nature.","t":"門票收入中很大一部分被用來保護森林，所以參觀公園也是在幫助大自然。"},{"w":"precede","p":"v.","d":"to happen before something else","c":"在……之前發生","s":"A long dry season precede the forest fire, so the trees and grass burned very quickly.","t":"森林大火之前經歷了一段漫長的乾季，所以樹木和草很快就燒起來了。"},{"w":"predominant","p":"adj.","d":"most common or strongest","c":"主要的；占優勢的","s":"Pine is the predominant tree in this forest, and it provides food for many squirrels and birds.","t":"松樹是這片森林中主要的樹種，它為許多松鼠和鳥類提供食物。"},{"w":"preliminary","p":"adj.","d":"coming before the main part; early","c":"初步的","s":"preliminary results show that the number of leopard cats has increased, but the final report will come out next year.","t":"初步結果顯示石虎的數量增加了，但最終報告將在明年發表。"},{"w":"presume","p":"v.","d":"to think something is true without proof","c":"推測；假定","s":"The rangers presume that the tiger crossed the river at night, because they found its footprints on the other side.","t":"巡山員推測老虎在夜間渡過了河，因為他們在對岸發現了牠的腳印。"},{"w":"priority","p":"n.","d":"something that is more important than other things","c":"優先事項","s":"Saving the last few kakapos is a top priority for New Zealand, so the government spends a lot on the project.","t":"拯救最後幾隻鴞鸚鵡是紐西蘭的首要優先事項，所以政府在這項計畫上投入了大量經費。"},{"w":"proceed","p":"v.","d":"to continue doing something","c":"繼續進行","s":"The building work cannot proceed until the birds leave their nests, so the company has to wait until autumn.","t":"在鳥兒離巢之前，建築工程無法繼續進行，所以公司必須等到秋天。"},{"w":"promote","p":"v.","d":"to help something grow or become popular","c":"促進；推廣","s":"The town wants to promote ecotourism, so it is training local young people to become nature guides.","t":"小鎮想要推廣生態旅遊，所以正在培訓當地年輕人成為自然導覽員。"},{"w":"prospect","p":"n.","d":"the possibility that something will happen","c":"前景；可能性","s":"The prospect of seeing wild whales attracts many tourists to Hualien, so boat companies there are very busy in summer.","t":"看到野生鯨魚的可能性吸引了許多遊客前往花蓮，所以那裡的船公司夏天都非常忙碌。"},{"w":"protocol","p":"n.","d":"a set of rules for how to do something","c":"規範程序；協議","s":"The rescue team follows a strict protocol when they handle sick animals, because some diseases can spread to humans.","t":"救援團隊在處理生病的動物時遵循嚴格的規範程序，因為有些疾病會傳染給人類。"},{"w":"publish","p":"v.","d":"to print or put information online for the public","c":"發表；出版","s":"The scientists will publish their research on dolphins next month, and they hope it will lead to better laws.","t":"科學家們將在下個月發表他們對海豚的研究，並希望這能帶來更好的法律。"},{"w":"pursue","p":"v.","d":"to try to achieve something over a long time","c":"追求；從事","s":"My cousin wants to pursue a career in marine biology, because she has loved sea animals since she was a child.","t":"我表姊想要從事海洋生物學的工作，因為她從小就熱愛海洋動物。"},{"w":"quantitative","p":"adj.","d":"based on numbers and amounts","c":"定量的；數量的","s":"The team collected quantitative data on the number of eggs in each nest, so they could compare the results with last year.","t":"團隊收集了每個巢中蛋數量的定量資料，這樣他們就能和去年的結果比較。"},{"w":"radical","p":"adj.","d":"very new and different; extreme","c":"激進的；徹底的","s":"Some experts believe we need radical changes in how we farm, because current methods are destroying too much wildlife.","t":"有些專家認為我們需要徹底改變耕作方式，因為目前的方法摧毀了太多野生動物。"},{"w":"ratio","p":"n.","d":"the relationship between two amounts","c":"比例；比率","s":"The ratio of male to female turtles is changing, because warmer sand produces more female babies.","t":"海龜的雄雌比例正在改變，因為較溫暖的沙子會孵出更多雌性小海龜。"},{"w":"rational","p":"adj.","d":"based on clear thinking, not feelings","c":"理性的","s":"We need a rational discussion about wild boars, because both the farmers and the animal lovers have strong feelings.","t":"我們需要對山豬進行理性的討論，因為農民和愛護動物人士雙方的情緒都很強烈。"},{"w":"recover","p":"v.","d":"to return to a normal or healthy state","c":"恢復；復原","s":"The forest will take fifty years to recover from the fire, but some small plants are already growing again.","t":"這片森林需要五十年才能從大火中恢復，但有些小植物已經開始重新生長了。"},{"w":"refine","p":"v.","d":"to improve something by making small changes","c":"改進；精煉","s":"The scientists refine their camera traps after the first test, so now the photos are much clearer at night.","t":"科學家們在第一次測試後改進了他們的自動相機，所以現在夜間的照片清晰許多。"},{"w":"region","p":"n.","d":"a large area of a country or the world","c":"地區；區域","s":"This region of Africa has the largest number of elephants, so it is a key area for the fight against poaching.","t":"非洲的這個地區擁有最多的大象，所以它是對抗盜獵的關鍵區域。"},{"w":"register","p":"v.","d":"to put a name on an official list","c":"登記；註冊","s":"All pet owners must register their reptiles with the city, so the government knows which animals are kept in homes.","t":"所有飼主都必須向市政府登記他們的爬蟲類寵物，這樣政府才知道哪些動物被飼養在家中。"},{"w":"reinforce","p":"v.","d":"to make something stronger","c":"加強；強化","s":"The farmers reinforce their fences with metal posts, because the wild boars had broken the old wooden ones.","t":"農民們用金屬柱加強了他們的圍籬，因為山豬已經撞壞了舊的木頭圍籬。"},{"w":"reject","p":"v.","d":"to refuse to accept something","c":"拒絕；否決","s":"The city council reject the plan to build a hotel on the beach, because it would destroy the turtles' nesting area.","t":"市議會否決了在海灘上蓋飯店的計畫，因為它會破壞海龜的築巢區。"},{"w":"release","p":"v.","d":"to let an animal go free","c":"釋放；野放","s":"After two months of care, the team release the eagle back into the mountains, and everyone cheered as it flew away.","t":"經過兩個月的照顧，團隊把老鷹野放回山林，當牠飛走時大家都歡呼了起來。"},{"w":"reluctant","p":"adj.","d":"not willing to do something","c":"不情願的","s":"Some farmers are reluctant to share their land with wild animals, because they worry about losing their crops.","t":"有些農民不情願和野生動物分享他們的土地，因為他們擔心失去農作物。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 7 (rely – submit)","cards":[{"w":"rely","p":"v.","d":"to need or depend on someone or something","c":"依賴；仰賴","s":"Many island birds rely on one type of fruit tree for food, so they will suffer if that tree disappears.","t":"許多島嶼鳥類仰賴單一種果樹作為食物，所以如果那種樹消失，牠們就會受苦。"},{"w":"require","p":"v.","d":"to need something","c":"需要；要求","s":"Looking after a baby elephant require a lot of time and money, because it drinks milk every three hours.","t":"照顧一隻小象需要大量的時間和金錢，因為牠每三個小時就要喝一次奶。"},{"w":"reside","p":"v.","d":"to live in a particular place","c":"居住","s":"About two hundred black bears reside in this national park, but they are rarely seen by hikers.","t":"大約有兩百隻黑熊居住在這座國家公園裡，但健行者很少看到牠們。"},{"w":"restore","p":"v.","d":"to bring something back to a good condition","c":"恢復；修復","s":"Volunteers are working to restore the old pond, so frogs and dragonflies can live there again.","t":"志工們正在努力修復那座舊池塘，讓青蛙和蜻蜓能再次在那裡生活。"},{"w":"reveal","p":"v.","d":"to show something that was hidden","c":"揭露；顯示","s":"The camera traps reveal that a rare cat lives in the forest, and the scientists were very excited by the news.","t":"自動相機揭露了森林裡住著一種稀有的貓科動物，科學家們對這個消息感到非常興奮。"},{"w":"revenue","p":"n.","d":"money that a business or government receives","c":"收入；營收","s":"The park uses its ticket revenue to pay the rangers, so tourism directly supports the protection of wildlife.","t":"公園用門票收入來支付巡山員的薪水，所以觀光直接支持了野生動物的保護。"},{"w":"reverse","p":"v.","d":"to change something back to how it was","c":"扭轉；逆轉","s":"It is not too late to reverse the loss of our forests, but we must start planting trees and stop cutting them down.","t":"要扭轉森林消失的趨勢還不算太晚，但我們必須開始種樹並停止砍伐。"},{"w":"revise","p":"v.","d":"to change something to improve or correct it","c":"修改；修訂","s":"Every five years, the experts revise the list of endangered species, and some animals are added while others are removed.","t":"專家每五年修訂一次瀕危物種名單，有些動物被加進去，而有些則被移除。"},{"w":"rigid","p":"adj.","d":"very strict and difficult to change","c":"嚴格的；死板的","s":"The rules in the protected area are rigid, so even scientists must ask for permission before they collect any plants.","t":"保護區內的規定非常嚴格，所以即使是科學家在採集任何植物前也必須申請許可。"},{"w":"route","p":"n.","d":"the way from one place to another","c":"路線","s":"The new railway will cut across the elephants' route to the river, so engineers are planning a tunnel for them.","t":"新鐵路將切斷大象前往河邊的路線，所以工程師正在為牠們規劃一條隧道。"},{"w":"scenario","p":"n.","d":"a possible situation in the future","c":"情境；可能的情況","s":"In the worst scenario, the island's rare birds could disappear within ten years, so action must be taken now.","t":"在最壞的情況下，島上的稀有鳥類可能在十年內消失，所以現在就必須採取行動。"},{"w":"scheme","p":"n.","d":"an official plan or programme","c":"計畫；方案","s":"Under the new scheme, farmers get money for every leopard cat seen on their land, so they now protect the animals.","t":"在新方案下，農民在自己的土地上每發現一隻石虎就能獲得獎金，所以他們現在都會保護這種動物。"},{"w":"scope","p":"n.","d":"the range of things that something covers","c":"範圍","s":"The scope of the study is quite small, because the scientists only looked at birds in one city park.","t":"這項研究的範圍相當小，因為科學家只觀察了一座城市公園裡的鳥。"},{"w":"secure","p":"v.","d":"to get something important after effort","c":"取得；爭取到","s":"The charity finally secure enough money to buy the forest, so it will never be cut down.","t":"那個慈善機構終於爭取到足夠的資金買下那片森林，所以它永遠不會被砍伐了。"},{"w":"seek","p":"v.","d":"to try to find or get something","c":"尋求；尋找","s":"During the drought, many animals sought water in nearby villages, which led to conflicts with farmers.","t":"乾旱期間，許多動物到附近村莊尋找水源，因而和農民發生衝突。"},{"w":"sequence","p":"n.","d":"a series of events in a particular order","c":"順序；一連串","s":"Scientists studied the sequence of events that led to the fish deaths, and they found that the problem began at a factory.","t":"科學家研究了導致魚群死亡的一連串事件，發現問題始於一家工廠。"},{"w":"series","p":"n.","d":"a number of similar things that come one after another","c":"系列；一連串","s":"The BBC made a nature series about the ocean, and it made millions of viewers care about plastic pollution.","t":"英國廣播公司製作了一部關於海洋的自然系列節目，讓數百萬觀眾開始關心塑膠汙染。"},{"w":"site","p":"n.","d":"a place where something is or happens","c":"地點；場所","s":"The beach is an important nesting site for green turtles, so it is closed to the public from May to October.","t":"這片海灘是綠蠵龜重要的築巢地點，所以從五月到十月不對外開放。"},{"w":"sole","p":"adj.","d":"only; single","c":"唯一的","s":"The kakapo's sole defence is to stay still and hide, but this does not work against cats and rats.","t":"鴞鸚鵡唯一的防禦方式就是靜止不動並躲藏，但這招對貓和老鼠沒有用。"},{"w":"somewhat","p":"adv.","d":"a little; to some degree","c":"有點；稍微","s":"The number of visitors has dropped somewhat since the new rules began, but the animals seem much calmer now.","t":"自從新規定實施以來，遊客人數稍微減少了，但動物們現在似乎平靜多了。"},{"w":"source","p":"n.","d":"the place where something comes from","c":"來源","s":"Insects are the main food source for many birds, so fewer insects means fewer birds in the countryside.","t":"昆蟲是許多鳥類主要的食物來源，所以昆蟲變少就代表鄉間的鳥類也會變少。"},{"w":"specific","p":"adj.","d":"exact and clear; particular","c":"特定的；明確的","s":"Each type of butterfly needs a specific plant to lay its eggs on, so gardeners should grow many kinds of local plants.","t":"每一種蝴蝶都需要一種特定的植物來產卵，所以園丁應該種植多種本地植物。"},{"w":"stable","p":"adj.","d":"not changing much; steady","c":"穩定的","s":"The number of gorillas in the park has been stable for five years, so the rangers feel hopeful about the future.","t":"公園裡大猩猩的數量五年來一直保持穩定，所以巡山員對未來感到有希望。"},{"w":"status","p":"n.","d":"official position or condition","c":"地位；狀態","s":"The giant panda's status changed from endangered to vulnerable in 2016, because its numbers had slowly increased.","t":"大貓熊的保育狀態在2016年從瀕危降為易危，因為牠們的數量已經慢慢增加了。"},{"w":"submit","p":"v.","d":"to give a document to someone for a decision","c":"提交；呈交","s":"Our class submit a proposal to the principal, and we asked for a small garden for bees and butterflies at school.","t":"我們班向校長提交了一份提案，請求在學校設置一座小型的蜜蜂和蝴蝶花園。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 8 (subsidy – bond)","cards":[{"w":"subsidy","p":"n.","d":"money a government pays to help reduce costs","c":"補貼；津貼","s":"Farmers who stop using pesticides can receive a subsidy from the government, so their income does not drop.","t":"停止使用農藥的農民可以獲得政府的補貼，讓他們的收入不會減少。"},{"w":"substitute","p":"n.","d":"something used instead of another thing","c":"替代品","s":"Scientists are developing a plant-based substitute for rhino horn, because they hope it will reduce the demand for real horns.","t":"科學家正在開發一種植物性的犀牛角替代品，因為他們希望這能減少對真犀牛角的需求。"},{"w":"supplement","p":"v.","d":"to add something to make it better or complete","c":"補充；增補","s":"In winter, the zoo supplement the birds' food with extra seeds, because there are fewer insects for them to eat.","t":"冬天時，動物園會用額外的種子來補充鳥的食物，因為可以吃的昆蟲變少了。"},{"w":"survive","p":"v.","d":"to continue to live, especially after danger","c":"存活；倖存","s":"Only a few baby turtles survive their first year, because so many animals in the sea want to eat them.","t":"只有少數幾隻小海龜能存活過第一年，因為海裡有太多動物想吃牠們。"},{"w":"suspend","p":"v.","d":"to stop something for a period of time","c":"暫停；中止","s":"The city suspend the building work near the lake, because a family of rare otters was found living there.","t":"市政府暫停了湖邊的建築工程，因為發現一家稀有的水獺住在那裡。"},{"w":"sustain","p":"v.","d":"to keep something alive or continuing","c":"維持；支撐","s":"The small forest cannot sustain so many deer, so the animals are eating all the young trees.","t":"這片小森林無法維持那麼多鹿的生存，所以這些動物正在吃光所有的小樹。"},{"w":"symbol","p":"n.","d":"something that represents an idea","c":"象徵；標誌","s":"The giant panda has become a symbol of wildlife protection, and its picture appears on the WWF logo.","t":"大貓熊已經成為野生動物保護的象徵，牠的圖案出現在世界自然基金會的標誌上。"},{"w":"target","p":"n.","d":"a goal you want to achieve","c":"目標","s":"The country set a target of protecting thirty percent of its land, and it hopes to reach this goal by 2030.","t":"這個國家設定了保護百分之三十國土的目標，並希望在2030年前達成。"},{"w":"temporary","p":"adj.","d":"lasting only for a short time","c":"暫時的；臨時的","s":"The injured deer was kept in a temporary shelter, and it was released once its leg had healed.","t":"受傷的鹿被安置在一個臨時收容所，等腿傷痊癒後就被野放了。"},{"w":"terminate","p":"v.","d":"to end something","c":"終止；結束","s":"The government terminate the company's fishing licence, because it had caught dolphins again and again.","t":"政府終止了那家公司的捕魚執照，因為它一再捕捉到海豚。"},{"w":"tradition","p":"n.","d":"a belief or custom passed down for many years","c":"傳統","s":"In some cultures, eating wild animals is an old tradition, so changing people's habits takes patience and respect.","t":"在某些文化中，吃野生動物是一種古老的傳統，所以改變人們的習慣需要耐心和尊重。"},{"w":"ultimate","p":"adj.","d":"final and most important","c":"最終的；終極的","s":"The ultimate goal of the breeding programme is to return the animals to the wild, not to keep them in zoos forever.","t":"繁殖計畫的最終目標是讓動物回歸野外，而不是讓牠們永遠待在動物園裡。"},{"w":"undergo","p":"v.","d":"to experience a process or change","c":"經歷；接受（治療等）","s":"The injured dolphin underwent surgery last week, and the vets say it is now eating and swimming normally.","t":"那隻受傷的海豚上週接受了手術，獸醫說牠現在已經能正常進食和游泳了。"},{"w":"underlie","p":"v.","d":"to be the real cause of something","c":"構成……的基礎；是……的根本原因","s":"Poverty often underlies the problem of poaching, because hunters need money to feed their families.","t":"貧窮往往是盜獵問題的根本原因，因為獵人需要錢來養家。"},{"w":"uniform","p":"adj.","d":"the same in all parts or at all times","c":"一致的；統一的","s":"There is no uniform rule for keeping exotic pets, because each country has its own laws.","t":"飼養奇特寵物並沒有統一的規定，因為每個國家都有自己的法律。"},{"w":"unique","p":"adj.","d":"being the only one of its kind","c":"獨特的；獨一無二的","s":"Every zebra has a unique pattern of stripes, so scientists can use photos to tell the animals apart.","t":"每隻斑馬都有獨一無二的條紋圖案，所以科學家可以用照片來區分牠們。"},{"w":"utilise","p":"v.","d":"to use something in an effective way","c":"利用；使用","s":"Rangers in the park now utilise smartphones to report poachers quickly, so help can arrive within minutes.","t":"園區的巡山員現在利用智慧型手機迅速通報盜獵者，讓支援能在幾分鐘內抵達。"},{"w":"vary","p":"v.","d":"to be different in different situations","c":"變化；不同","s":"The size of a bear's territory can vary a lot, because it depends on how much food is available.","t":"熊的領域大小可能差異很大，因為這取決於有多少可取得的食物。"},{"w":"violate","p":"v.","d":"to break a law or rule","c":"違反；違背","s":"The tour company violate the rules by getting too close to the whales, so it had to pay a large fine.","t":"那家旅遊公司因為太靠近鯨魚而違反規定，所以必須支付一大筆罰款。"},{"w":"visible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be seen","c":"看得見的；明顯的","s":"The damage from the oil spill was clearly visible from the air, and black water stretched for kilometres along the coast.","t":"漏油造成的損害從空中清楚可見，黑色的海水沿著海岸延伸了好幾公里。"},{"w":"voluntary","p":"adj.","d":"done because you choose to, not because you must","c":"自願的","s":"The beach clean-up is voluntary, but more than two hundred students joined it last Saturday.","t":"淨灘活動是自願參加的，但上週六有超過兩百名學生加入。"},{"w":"welfare","p":"n.","d":"the health and happiness of people or animals","c":"福利；福祉","s":"Good zoos care about the welfare of their animals, so they give them large spaces and a natural diet.","t":"好的動物園關心動物的福祉，所以會給牠們寬敞的空間和自然的飲食。"},{"w":"accelerate","p":"v.","d":"to happen or make happen faster","c":"加速","s":"Warmer weather has accelerate the melting of the Arctic ice, so polar bears have less time to hunt each year.","t":"較暖的天氣加速了北極冰層的融化，所以北極熊每年能狩獵的時間變少了。"},{"w":"decade","p":"n.","d":"a period of ten years","c":"十年","s":"Over the last decade, the number of black-faced spoonbills has more than doubled, thanks to the hard work of many countries.","t":"在過去十年間，黑面琵鷺的數量增加了一倍以上，這要歸功於許多國家的努力。"},{"w":"bond","p":"n.","d":"a close connection between people or animals","c":"聯繫；情感連結","s":"The bond between a mother orangutan and her baby is very strong, because the baby stays with her for about eight years.","t":"紅毛猩猩媽媽和寶寶之間的情感連結非常緊密，因為寶寶會和媽媽待在一起大約八年。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"Fixed Phrases & Collocations 固定片語與搭配詞","cards":[{"w":"on the brink of extinction","p":"adj.phr.","d":"very close to disappearing forever","c":"瀕臨滅絕","s":"The vaquita porpoise is on the brink of extinction, because only about ten of them are left in the sea near Mexico.","t":"小頭鼠海豚瀕臨滅絕，因為墨西哥附近的海域只剩下大約十隻。"},{"w":"in the wild","p":"phr.","d":"living free in nature, not in a zoo","c":"在野外","s":"Pandas live for about twenty years in the wild, but they can live longer in zoos because they get medical care.","t":"貓熊在野外大約能活二十年，但在動物園裡因為能得到醫療照顧，所以可以活得更久。"},{"w":"food chain","p":"n.phr.","d":"the order in which animals eat other plants and animals","c":"食物鏈","s":"Sharks are at the top of the ocean food chain, so when they disappear, the whole sea can become unbalanced.","t":"鯊魚位於海洋食物鏈的頂端，所以當牠們消失時，整個海洋都可能失去平衡。"},{"w":"natural habitat","p":"n.phr.","d":"the place where an animal normally lives in nature","c":"自然棲地","s":"The zoo tries to make the gorillas' home look like their natural habitat, so it has planted tall trees and thick bushes.","t":"動物園試著讓大猩猩的家看起來像牠們的自然棲地，所以種了高大的樹木和茂密的灌木。"},{"w":"habitat loss","p":"n.phr.","d":"the destruction of the places where animals live","c":"棲地喪失","s":"habitat loss is the biggest danger for orangutans, because their forests are being replaced by palm oil farms.","t":"棲地喪失是紅毛猩猩面臨的最大危險，因為牠們的森林正被棕櫚油農園取代。"},{"w":"climate change","p":"n.phr.","d":"long-term changes in the Earth's weather and temperature","c":"氣候變遷","s":"climate change is making the sea warmer, so many corals are dying and fish are moving to cooler waters.","t":"氣候變遷正使海水變暖，所以許多珊瑚正在死亡，魚群也正移往較涼的水域。"},{"w":"keystone species","p":"n.phr.","d":"an animal that many other species depend on","c":"關鍵物種","s":"The sea otter is a keystone species, because it eats sea urchins that would otherwise destroy the kelp forests.","t":"海獺是一種關鍵物種，因為牠會吃掉海膽，否則海膽會摧毀海藻森林。"},{"w":"human-wildlife conflict","p":"n.phr.","d":"problems that happen when people and wild animals meet","c":"人與野生動物的衝突","s":"human-wildlife conflict is growing in Kenya, because more farms are being built on land where elephants used to walk.","t":"人與野生動物的衝突在肯亞日益加劇，因為越來越多農場蓋在大象過去行走的土地上。"},{"w":"die out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to disappear completely","c":"絕跡；滅絕","s":"The dodo die out in the 1600s, because sailors hunted it and the animals they brought ate its eggs.","t":"渡渡鳥在十七世紀絕跡了，因為水手們獵捕牠，而他們帶來的動物則吃掉了牠的蛋。"},{"w":"wipe out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to destroy or kill something completely","c":"徹底消滅","s":"A single disease could wipe out the whole population of Tasmanian devils, so scientists keep some healthy ones on a safe island.","t":"單一種疾病就可能徹底消滅所有的袋獾，所以科學家把一些健康的袋獾養在一座安全的島上。"},{"w":"pose a threat to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be a danger to something","c":"對……構成威脅","s":"Stray cats pose a threat to the small birds on the island, because they hunt them day and night.","t":"流浪貓對島上的小鳥構成威脅，因為牠們日夜都在獵捕鳥類。"},{"w":"make a comeback","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become common or successful again","c":"捲土重來；重新出現","s":"The bald eagle has make a comeback in the United States, because the harmful pesticide DDT was banned in 1972.","t":"白頭海鵰已經在美國重新出現，因為有害的農藥DDT在1972年被禁用了。"},{"w":"strike a balance","p":"v.phr.","d":"to find a fair middle point between two things","c":"取得平衡","s":"The town is trying to strike a balance between tourism and nature, so it limits the number of boats near the dolphins.","t":"小鎮正努力在觀光與自然之間取得平衡，所以限制了靠近海豚的船隻數量。"},{"w":"under threat","p":"phr.","d":"in danger of being harmed or destroyed","c":"受到威脅","s":"Many wetlands in Asia are under threat from new buildings, so migrating birds are losing their resting places.","t":"亞洲許多濕地正受到新建築的威脅，所以遷徙的鳥類正逐漸失去牠們的休息地。"},{"w":"at risk of","p":"phr.","d":"likely to suffer something bad","c":"有……的危險","s":"Without help, the Formosan leopard cat is at risk of disappearing from Taiwan, so people must drive slowly on mountain roads.","t":"如果沒有協助，石虎有從台灣消失的危險，所以人們在山區道路上必須慢慢開車。"},{"w":"take action","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something to solve a problem","c":"採取行動","s":"If we do not take action now, our children may only see tigers in books, so everyone should help in small ways.","t":"如果我們現在不採取行動，我們的孩子可能只能在書中看到老虎，所以每個人都應該盡一點小小的心力。"},{"w":"a drop in the ocean","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very small amount compared with what is needed","c":"杯水車薪；滄海一粟","s":"One beach clean-up may seem like a drop in the ocean, but if everyone joins in, the difference can be huge.","t":"一次淨灘看起來也許只是杯水車薪，但如果每個人都參與，差別就會非常大。"},{"w":"turn a blind eye to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to pretend not to notice something wrong","c":"視而不見；睜一隻眼閉一隻眼","s":"Some officers turn a blind eye to the illegal pet shops, so the animal trade continues in the city.","t":"有些官員對非法寵物店視而不見，所以動物交易在城市裡持續進行。"},{"w":"the balance of nature","p":"n.phr.","d":"the natural state in which plants and animals live together steadily","c":"自然平衡；生態平衡","s":"When wolves were removed from the park, the balance of nature was broken, and the deer ate too many young trees.","t":"當狼被移出公園後，生態平衡就被破壞了，鹿吃掉了太多小樹。"},{"w":"dead as a dodo","p":"adj.phr.","d":"completely gone or no longer existing","c":"徹底消失的；過時的","s":"If we keep cutting down the rainforest, many amazing animals will soon be dead as a dodo, and we can never bring them back.","t":"如果我們持續砍伐雨林，許多令人驚嘆的動物很快就會徹底消失，而且我們再也無法讓牠們回來。"}]}];
